      "name": "BinkFileReadSynchronized",
      "signature": "dword BinkFileReadSynchronized(BinkFileHandle * pBinkFile, int nFileOffset, void * pReadBuffer, dword dwRequestSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD",
      "comment": "Performs synchronized file read operation for Bink video files with automatic positioning and buffer management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Increment lock counter at offset 0x5c using atomic operation to enter critical section\n2. Wait for background operations to complete by polling wait condition at offset 0x60\n   - Loop with Sleep(0) to yield CPU time while waiting\n   - Call BinkService on video context at offset 0x18 to process pending operations\n3. If offset parameter is valid (-1 means use current position):\n   - Check if file position at offset 0x4c differs from requested offset\n   - Set file pointer to base offset (0x74) + requested offset using SetFilePointer\n   - Update current position tracker at offset 0x4c\n4. Execute file read using ReadFile with specified buffer and byte count\n   - Use file handle at offset 0x48\n   - Store actual bytes read in return variable\n5. Update file position tracking:\n   - Add bytes read to current position at offset 0x4c  \n   - Copy updated position to secondary tracker at offset 0x50\n6. Calculate available buffer space:\n   - Compute remaining bytes: end position (0x78) - current position (0x4c)\n   - Take minimum of remaining bytes and buffer size limit (0x38)\n   - Store available space at offset 0x40 for next operation\n7. Decrement lock counter using atomic operation to exit critical section\n\nParameters:\n\npBinkFile: BinkFileHandle * - File context structure containing handles, positions, and synchronization state\nnFileOffset: int - Target file offset for read operation, or -1 to use current position\npReadBuffer: void * - Destination buffer for read data\ndwRequestSize: dword - Number of bytes to read from file\n\nReturns:\n\ndword - Number of bytes actually read from file (same as ReadFile output parameter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nOffset value -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) indicates current file position should be used without seeking.\nFunction provides thread-safe access using atomic increment/decrement of lock counter.\nBinkService integration ensures video operations don't conflict with file I/O.\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type     Description\n------  ----  --------------- -------  ---------------------------\n0x18    4     pBinkService    void **  Pointer to Bink service context for video processing  \n0x38    4     dwBufferSize    dword    Maximum buffer size limit for read operations\n0x40    4     dwAvailable     dword    Available buffer space for next read operation\n0x48    4     hFile           HANDLE   Windows file handle for I/O operations\n0x4c    4     dwCurrentPos    dword    Current file position tracker (primary)\n0x50    4     dwPositionCopy  dword    Secondary file position tracker (backup/copy)\n0x5c    1     bLockCounter    byte     Atomic lock counter for thread synchronization\n0x60    4     nWaitCondition  int      Background operation wait condition flag\n0x74    4     dwBaseOffset    dword    Base file offset for positioning calculations\n0x78    4     dwEndPosition   dword    End of file position for bounds checking",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
