      "name": "BinkFileClose",
      "signature": "uint BinkFileClose(int * pFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Performs synchronized file I/O operation with optional throttling control and statistics tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire exclusive access using atomic increment operations on read/write counters at offsets 0x60 and 0x5c\n2. Check if both counters equal 1 to ensure exclusive access; set error flag if not\n3. If exclusive access achieved, validate buffer availability (minimum 4KB buffer space and read-ahead space)\n4. If insufficient buffer space, copy current buffer position to base position for next read\n5. Otherwise, record start time and set I/O active flag at offset 0x1c\n6. Execute ReadFile() operation reading 4KB (0x1000 bytes) into current buffer position\n7. Clear I/O active flag and update read statistics: total bytes read, current position, buffer pointer\n8. Handle buffer wraparound when buffer pointer exceeds end boundary by resetting to base\n9. Update remaining buffer space and advance base position by bytes read\n10. Update maximum position reached if current position exceeds previous maximum\n11. If throttling rate specified (offset 0x7c), calculate required delay and sleep to maintain rate\n12. Record end time and calculate elapsed milliseconds for this I/O operation\n13. Update total I/O time and categorize as foreground/background time based on file position state\n14. Release exclusive access by atomic decrement of read/write counters\n15. If error occurred during access acquisition, yield CPU time slice via Sleep(0)\n\nParameters:\npFileHandle - Pointer to BinkFileHandle structure containing file state, buffers, and I/O configuration\n\nReturns:\nNumber of bytes read from file on success\n0xFFFFFFFF on error (failed to acquire exclusive access)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Minimum buffer requirement: 4KB free space and 4KB read-ahead space\n- Buffer wraparound: when buffer pointer exceeds end boundary, wraps to base address\n- Throttling: optional rate limiting using millisecond delays based on bytes/time ratio\n- Statistics tracking: separate foreground/background I/O time counters based on file position\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type  | Description\n0x1c   | 4    | dwIoActiveFlag      | uint  | I/O operation in progress flag\n0x20   | 4    | dwTotalBytesRead    | uint  | Cumulative bytes read counter\n0x24   | 4    | nFilePosition       | int   | Current file position marker\n0x28   | 4    | dwTotalIoTime       | uint  | Total I/O operation time in ms\n0x30   | 4    | dwForegroundIoTime  | uint  | Foreground I/O time in ms\n0x34   | 4    | dwBackgroundIoTime  | uint  | Background I/O time in ms\n0x3c   | 4    | dwMaxPositionReached| uint  | Maximum file position accessed\n0x40   | 4    | dwBufferBase        | uint  | Buffer base position\n0x44   | 4    | dwCurrentPosition   | uint  | Current buffer position\n0x48   | 4    | hFileHandle         | HANDLE| Win32 file handle for ReadFile()\n0x4c   | 4    | dwCurrentFilePos    | uint  | Current file read position\n0x58   | 4    | dwRemainingBuffer   | uint  | Remaining buffer space\n0x5c   | 4    | nWriteCounter       | int   | Atomic write operation counter\n0x60   | 4    | nReadCounter        | int   | Atomic read operation counter\n0x64   | 4    | pBufferBase         | void* | Base address of circular buffer\n0x68   | 4    | pBufferEnd          | void* | End boundary of circular buffer\n0x6c   | 4    | pCurrentBufferPtr   | void* | Current write position in buffer\n0x78   | 4    | dwFileEndPosition   | uint  | End position of file data\n0x7c   | 4    | dwThrottleRate      | uint  | Optional throttling rate (bytes/ms)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1000 (4096) - Standard I/O block size in bytes\n0x3e8 (1000) - Milliseconds per second for throttle calculation\n0xFFFFFFFF - Error return value indicating access failure",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
