      "name": "InverseDiscreteCosineTransform",
      "signature": "void InverseDiscreteCosineTransform(byte * pOutputBuffer, uint dwRowStride, short * pInputCoefficients, int * pCosineTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs Inverse Discrete Cosine Transform (IDCT) on an 8x8 block of coefficients.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointers to input coefficients and output workspace buffer\n2. Process 8 columns in first phase (frequency domain to spatial domain):\n   a. Check if column has only DC component (all AC coefficients zero)\n   b. If DC-only: Set all 8 values to scaled DC coefficient\n   c. If has AC components: Perform full 1D IDCT using butterfly operations\n   d. Scale intermediate results by cosine table values and shift right by 11 bits\n   e. Store transformed column values in temporary workspace buffer\n3. Process 8 rows in second phase (complete spatial domain conversion):\n   a. Apply 1D IDCT to workspace buffer rows using butterfly operations\n   b. Add 0x7F bias for proper unsigned byte conversion\n   c. Right shift by 8 bits to convert to byte range (0-255)\n   d. Store final pixel values in output buffer with row stride\n\nParameters:\nparam_1 (int): Output image buffer pointer (treated as byte* in assembly)\nparam_2 (int): Row stride in bytes for output buffer\nparam_3 (short*): Input DCT coefficients array [8x8 shorts]\nparam_4 (int*): Cosine lookup table for IDCT calculations\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function stores results directly in output buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DC-only blocks (no AC coefficients): Optimized path fills entire block with single value\n- Full IDCT uses butterfly algorithm with magic constants for rotation factors\n- Final bias of 0x7F ensures proper rounding for unsigned byte conversion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xb50 (2896): Cosine rotation factor for butterfly operations  \n0xec8 (3784): Cosine rotation factor for butterfly operations\n0x14e8 (-5352): Negative cosine rotation factor for butterfly operations\n0x8a9 (2217): Cosine rotation factor for butterfly operations\n0xb (11): Right shift amount for fixed-point arithmetic scaling\n0x7f (127): Bias added before final byte conversion\n0x8 (8): Right shift amount for final byte range conversion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:5f0e8986d47e0e2dd68f6e1c8727a19aff82db1624719320872a2053b5cb9674",
