      "name": "DetectD3DCapabilities",
      "signature": "void DetectD3DCapabilities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Detects D3D/DirectDraw capabilities and configures global capability flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 316-byte D3DCaps structure with zero values\n2. Set structure size field to 0x13c (316 bytes)  \n3. Query D3D device capabilities via virtual function call at offset 0x2c\n4. Process capability flags from offset 0x4 (dwCapabilityFlags) using bit tests:\n   - Extract texture format capabilities to g_dwD3DCapFlags1\n   - Extract additional format capabilities to g_dwD3DCapFlags2\n5. Initialize 32-byte structure for video memory query\n6. Query video memory via virtual function call at offset 0x54\n7. Calculate and store video memory size (shifted right by 3)\n8. Get system display metrics (width, height, color depth)\n9. Calculate total color depth as width * height * bits_per_pixel\n10. Set Bink flags based on color depth:\n    - If 8-bit color: Set g_dwBinkFlags to 0xfd (limited color)\n    - Otherwise: Calculate capability result and store in g_dwBinkFlags\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results stored in global variables:\n- g_dwD3DCapFlags1: Primary capability flags\n- g_dwD3DCapFlags2: Secondary capability flags  \n- g_dwVideoMemory: Available video memory in KB\n- g_nScreenWidth: Screen width in pixels\n- g_nScreenHeight: Screen height in pixels\n- g_nPixelDepth: Total color depth (width * height * bpp)\n- g_dwBinkFlags: Bink video playback capability flags\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf color depth is 8 bits per pixel, sets g_dwBinkFlags to 0xfd indicating limited color support\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x13c - Size of D3DCaps structure (316 bytes)\n0x2c - Virtual function offset for capability query\n0x54 - Virtual function offset for video memory query  \n0x800000 - Capability bit for texture format support\n0x1000000 - Capability bit for advanced texture formats\n0x80000 - Capability bit for 16-bit texture support\n0x100000 - Capability bit for 24-bit texture support\n0x2000000 - Capability bit for 32-bit texture support\n0x4000000 - Capability bit for alpha texture support\n0x200000 - Capability bit for compressed texture support\n0x400000 - Capability bit for bump mapping support\n0x4000 - Secondary capability bit\n0x8000 - Secondary capability bit  \n0x400 - Secondary capability bit for filtering\n0x800 - Secondary capability bit for blending\n0x10000 - Secondary capability bit for mipmapping\n0x20000 - Secondary capability bit for perspective correction\n0x1000 - Secondary capability bit for color keying\n0x2000 - Secondary capability bit for fog support\n0xfd - Bink flag value for 8-bit color mode\n0xe - GetDeviceCaps parameter for horizontal resolution\n0xc - GetDeviceCaps parameter for vertical resolution",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
