      "name": "InitializeDirectDraw",
      "signature": "void InitializeDirectDraw(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize DirectDraw graphics library for application use.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Temporarily disable Windows error reporting with SetErrorMode(SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX)\n2. Attempt to load DDRAW.DLL library using LoadLibraryA\n3. Store the module handle in g_hDirectDrawModule global variable\n4. Restore original error reporting mode with SetErrorMode\n5. Verify module handle is valid (greater than 0x1F indicates success)\n6. If library loaded successfully, get DirectDrawCreate function address via GetProcAddress\n7. Store function pointer in g_pfnDirectDrawCreate global variable\n8. If DirectDrawCreate function found, initialization complete and return\n9. If DirectDrawCreate function not found, free the loaded library with FreeLibrary\n10. Set g_hDirectDrawModule to 1 as fallback value indicating DirectDraw unavailable\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function always succeeds, uses global variables to indicate DirectDraw availability\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DDRAW.DLL fails to load (handle <= 0x1F), sets fallback value 1 in g_hDirectDrawModule\n- If DirectDrawCreate function not found in loaded library, frees library and sets fallback\n- Error mode 0x8000 (SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX) prevents system error dialogs during library loading\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8000: SEM_NOOPENFILEERRORBOX flag to suppress Windows error dialogs\n- 0x1F: Minimum valid Windows module handle value (LoadLibraryA returns > 31 for success)\n- 0x1: Fallback value indicating DirectDraw initialization failed\n\nError Handling:\n- Library load failure: No exception thrown, fallback value set in global\n- Missing function: Library freed, fallback value set in global\n- All error conditions handled gracefully without throwing exceptions",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
