      "name": "RestoreDisplaySettingsIfLastReference",
      "signature": "void RestoreDisplaySettingsIfLastReference(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reference-counted display mode restoration for Bink video subsystem\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement the global display mode reference counter\n2. Check if reference counter reached zero AND display mode was previously changed\n3. If both conditions are true, clear the display mode changed flag\n4. Call ChangeDisplaySettingsA to restore default desktop display settings with CDS_FULLSCREEN flag\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs cleanup without return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction only restores display settings when BOTH conditions are met:\n- Reference counter reaches exactly zero (no remaining Bink contexts)\n- Display mode changed flag is non-zero (settings were previously modified)\nEarly exit if reference counter is still positive or no changes were made\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4 (CDS_FULLSCREEN) - ChangeDisplaySettingsA flag to restore fullscreen display mode\n\nError Handling:\nNo error handling - assumes ChangeDisplaySettingsA succeeds\nCalled during cleanup paths where failure cannot be recovered\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_dwDisplayModeReferenceCount (0x1002f150) - Reference counter for active display mode contexts\ng_dwDisplayModeChanged (0x1002f14c) - Flag indicating whether display settings were modified",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3b88190d8567fb006c5e63e9ee334ba4152321ba4af6876da20a59ab9e7350d2",
