      "name": "CreateDirectDrawSurface",
      "signature": "uint CreateDirectDrawSurface(IDirectDraw * pDDInterface, uint dwWidth, uint dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Creates a DirectDraw surface for video rendering using the provided interface and dimensions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize local surface descriptor buffer with zeroes (0x1b DWORDs = 108 bytes)\n2. Set up surface descriptor structure with magic values (0x6c, 0x1007) \n3. Configure surface parameters: flags (0x4080), dimensions, pixel depth (0x20), bit depth (4)\n4. Call DirectDraw interface method at offset 0x18 to validate the interface\n5. If validation fails, return 0 (failure)\n6. Call DirectDraw surface creation method at offset 0x64 with descriptor parameters\n7. If surface creation fails, call cleanup method at offset 0x8 and return 0\n8. Call FUN_10006b90 to configure the created surface with rendering parameters\n9. Call DirectDraw interface method at offset 0x80 to finalize surface setup\n10. Return surface flags value (0x20) indicating success\n\nParameters:\n- pDDInterface: Pointer to DirectDraw interface object for surface creation\n- dwWidth: Surface width in pixels for the video buffer\n- dwHeight: Surface height in pixels for the video buffer\n\nReturns:\n- 0x20 (32): Success - surface created and configured successfully\n- 0: Failure - DirectDraw interface validation or surface creation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DirectDraw interface validation at offset 0x18 must succeed before surface creation\n- Surface creation method at offset 0x64 uses specific descriptor format\n- Cleanup method at offset 0x8 is called only on surface creation failure\n- Surface configuration method at offset 0x80 finalizes the surface setup\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x6c (108): Surface descriptor structure size in bytes\n- 0x1007: Surface descriptor format identifier or flags\n- 0x4080: Surface creation flags (likely DDSD_CAPS | DDSD_PIXELFORMAT | DDSD_WIDTH | DDSD_HEIGHT)\n- 0x20 (32): Pixel format value, possibly 32-bit color depth or RGB format\n- 4: Bit depth parameter for pixel format configuration\n- 0x18 (24): DirectDraw interface validation method offset\n- 0x64 (100): DirectDraw surface creation method offset  \n- 0x8 (8): DirectDraw interface cleanup/release method offset\n- 0x80 (128): DirectDraw surface finalization method offset",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
