      "name": "DetectPixelFormatAndGetRGBMasks",
      "signature": "char DetectPixelFormatAndGetRGBMasks(HDC hdc, uint * pRgbMasks)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Detects display pixel format and retrieves RGB bit masks for current device context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read video memory type from g_dwVideoMemory global variable\n2. If video memory type > 2 (24/32-bit), set standard 32-bit RGB masks (0xff0000, 0xff00, 0xff)\n3. Return format code 1 if video memory type != 3, otherwise return format code 2\n4. Initialize BITMAPINFO structure array on stack (0x428 bytes for 24 structures)\n5. Create temporary 1x1 compatible bitmap using CreateCompatibleBitmap()\n6. If bitmap creation succeeds, call GetDIBits() twice to populate BITMAPINFO structure\n7. Check compression type and red color mask to determine 16-bit format:\n   - If compression == 3 (BI_BITFIELDS) and red mask == 0xf800, use 16-bit 565 format\n   - Set RGB masks (0xf800, 0x7e0, 0x1f) and return format code 4\n8. For all other cases, assume 15-bit 555 format\n9. Set RGB masks (0x7c00, 0x3e0, 0x1f) and return format code 3\n10. Clean up temporary bitmap with DeleteObject()\n\nParameters:\nhdc: Device context handle for the target display device\npRgbMasks: Pointer to array of 3 uint values to receive RGB bit masks (red, green, blue)\n\nReturns:\nchar value indicating detected pixel format:\n- 1: 32-bit format when g_dwVideoMemory != 3\n- 2: 32-bit format when g_dwVideoMemory == 3  \n- 3: 15-bit 555 format (5-5-5 RGB)\n- 4: 16-bit 565 format (5-6-5 RGB)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If CreateCompatibleBitmap() fails, defaults to 15-bit 555 format\n- GetDIBits() called twice to ensure BITMAPINFO structure is properly populated\n- Uses BI_BITFIELDS compression check to distinguish 16-bit formats\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xff0000: 32-bit red mask (bits 16-23)\n- 0xff00: 32-bit green mask (bits 8-15) \n- 0xff: 32-bit blue mask (bits 0-7)\n- 0xf800: 16-bit 565 red mask (bits 11-15)\n- 0x7e0: 16-bit 565 green mask (bits 5-10)\n- 0x1f: 16-bit blue mask (bits 0-4)\n- 0x7c00: 15-bit 555 red mask (bits 10-14)\n- 0x3e0: 15-bit 555 green mask (bits 5-9)\n- 0x28: Size of BITMAPINFOHEADER structure (40 bytes)\n- 0x10a: Loop counter for clearing BITMAPINFO array (266 DWORDs = 1064 bytes)\n- 3: BI_BITFIELDS compression type constant\n\nStructure Layout:\ntagBITMAPINFO array (1056 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0x000  | 40   | bmiHeader  | BITMAPINFOHEADER | Bitmap header with format info\n0x028  | 4    | bmiColors[0] | RGBQUAD | First color table entry (used for masks)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
