      "name": "InitializeBinkVideoPlayback",
      "signature": "int * InitializeBinkVideoPlayback(uint param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "BinkDecoder *",
      "comment": "InitializeBinkVideoPlayback - Completes initialization of a Bink video context\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates frame rate against buffer configuration using multiplication overflow check\n2. Sets high-performance playback flags (0x2000) if frame rate threshold exceeded\n3. Branches based on playback mode:\n   - Standard mode: Tracks memory allocation and sets up memory pointers for streaming\n   - High-performance mode: Allocates cache buffers and initializes file I/O callbacks\n4. Initializes buffer boundaries with null terminator at data region end\n5. Sets frame index to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) indicating no frame currently loaded\n6. Calculates playback timing based on frame rate (default 2000ms if rate is 0)\n7. Positions first frame via BinkPositionFrame\n8. Records start timestamp via timeGetTime for playback synchronization\n9. Drains any pending file I/O operations in standard mode\n10. Selects audio track based on flags and global audio selection\n11. If audio enabled: initializes sound buffer, allocates audio memory via RadMalloc\n12. Configures audio context via InitializeBinkAudioContext\n13. Creates background thread for frame decoding via CreateThreadWithParamBlock\n14. Returns context pointer on success, NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n    dwFrameRateLimit (ECX) - Maximum frame rate threshold for high-performance mode\n    dwBufferConfig (EDX) - Buffer size configuration multiplier\n    IMPLICIT in_EAX - Base value for overflow calculation\n    IMPLICIT unaff_EBX - Pointer to AllocContext being initialized\n    IMPLICIT unaff_EBP - Stack frame pointer with additional configuration data\n\nReturns:\n    AllocContext* - Initialized video playback context on success\n    NULL (0) - On memory allocation failure or thread creation failure\n\nError Handling:\n    Sets BinkSetError(\"Out of memory.\") on allocation failure\n    Calls cleanup callback at [EBP-0x2AC] before returning NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n    0x2000 - High-performance playback mode flag\n    0x200000 - Skip file I/O drain flag\n    0x4000000 - Skip cleanup callback flag  \n    0x8000000 - Background thread required flag\n    0x4000 - Audio track selection flag\n    0x7D0 (2000) - Default timing interval in milliseconds\n    0x2EE (750) - Audio timing adjustment constant\n    0x3E8 (1000) - Milliseconds conversion factor\n\nStructure Offsets (AllocContext via EBX):\n    +0x008 - Total frames count\n    +0x00C - Current frame index (-1 = none)\n    +0x014 - Frame rate numerator\n    +0x018 - Frame rate denominator\n    +0x020 - Playback flags\n    +0x028 - Buffer size\n    +0x0F0 - Audio track count\n    +0x100 - Thread handle\n    +0x108 - High-performance buffer pointer\n    +0x10C - File descriptor pointer\n    +0x114 - Read callback function pointer\n    +0x11C - Seek callback function pointer\n    +0x120 - I/O poll callback function pointer\n    +0x124 - Close callback function pointer\n    +0x1DC - Streaming buffer size\n    +0x1D8 - Streaming buffer pointer\n    +0x1E8 - Selected audio track index\n    +0x1F0 - Audio track info array pointer\n    +0x1EC - Audio track size array pointer\n    +0x22C - Audio enabled flag\n    +0x230 - Initialized flag\n    +0x244 - Start timestamp\n    +0x280 - Audio buffer size (aligned to 256)\n    +0x284 - Audio buffer start\n    +0x288 - Audio buffer end\n    +0x294 - Audio context pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
