      "name": "UpdateFrameTimingStatistics",
      "signature": "void UpdateFrameTimingStatistics(BinkDecoder * pDecoder, uint dwCurrentTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates frame timing statistics for Bink video decoder performance tracking\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if last frame start time (offset 0x218) is valid (non-zero)\n2. Calculate elapsed time since last frame (dwCurrentTime - last frame time)\n3. Clear the last frame start time field (reset to 0 for next measurement)\n4. Compare elapsed time against current maximum frame time (offset 0x21c)\n5. If new elapsed time exceeds current maximum:\n   - Save current maximum as second-best time (0x21c -> 0x224) \n   - Update maximum frame time with new elapsed time\n   - Save associated frame data (0x220 -> 0x228, 0xc -> 0x220)\n6. Otherwise, check if elapsed time exceeds second-best time (offset 0x224)\n7. If so, update second-best time and save associated frame data\n\nParameters:\n  pDecoder (BinkDecoder *): Pointer to Bink decoder context containing timing statistics\n  dwCurrentTime (uint): Current timestamp for frame timing calculations\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nStructure Layout (BinkDecoder timing fields):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n  0x00c   4     dwFrameData       uint    Current frame identifier/data\n  0x218   4     dwLastFrameStart  uint    Last frame start timestamp (0=invalid)\n  0x21c   4     dwMaxFrameTime    uint    Maximum frame processing time recorded\n  0x220   4     dwMaxFrameData    uint    Frame data associated with maximum time\n  0x224   4     dwSecondBestTime  uint    Second longest frame processing time\n  0x228   4     dwSecondBestData  uint    Frame data for second longest time\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwLastFrameStart is 0, no timing update occurs (first call or reset state)\n  - Statistics track the two worst frame processing times for performance analysis\n  - Used by BinkWait, BinkGetRealtime, and other timing-sensitive Bink functions",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
