      "name": "BinkService",
      "signature": "void BinkService(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Conditionally processes Bink video frames based on decoder state\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if BinkDecoder service flag at offset 0x1e8 is active (not -1)\n2. If service flag indicates processing needed, call ProcessBinkFrame\n3. If service flag is -1 (inactive), skip processing and return\n\nParameters:\npBinkDecoder (BinkDecoder *): Pointer to Bink video decoder context structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return a value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nService flag value -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Indicates no frame processing needed\nService flag value != -1: Indicates frame processing required\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1e8 (488): Offset to service processing flag in BinkDecoder structure\n-1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Inactive/disabled state marker for service flag",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
