      "name": "BinkSetPan",
      "signature": "void BinkSetPan(BinkDecoder * pBinkDecoder, int nPanValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Set audio panning for Bink video decoder if valid and callback available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pBinkDecoder parameter is not null\n2. Check decoder state field at offset 0x1e8 is not -1 (inactive)\n3. Retrieve function pointer from offset 0x2b4 (pan callback)\n4. If callback exists, call it with decoder base address (offset 0x2a4) and pan value\n5. Return (void function)\n\nParameters:\n- pBinkDecoder (BinkDecoder *): Pointer to BinkDecoder structure containing state and callbacks\n- nPanValue (int): Pan value to set (range and format determined by callback implementation)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pBinkDecoder: Function returns immediately without action\n- Decoder state -1: Function returns immediately (decoder inactive/uninitialized)\n- Null callback pointer: Function returns immediately (pan feature not available)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type      | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-----------|------------------------------------------\n0x1e8  | 4    | DecoderState    | int       | Decoder status (-1 = inactive)\n0x2a4  | ?    | CallbackBase    | void *    | Base address passed to callbacks\n0x2b4  | 4    | PanCallback     | void (*)(void *, int) | Function pointer for pan control\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1e8 (488): Offset to decoder state field\n- 0x2a4 (676): Offset to callback base address\n- 0x2b4 (692): Offset to pan callback function pointer\n- -1: Inactive/uninitialized decoder state value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
