      "name": "BinkGetTrackID",
      "signature": "int BinkGetTrackID(BinkHandle * pBinkHandle, int nTrackIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves a track ID from a Bink video file handle using an index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that the Bink handle pointer is not NULL\n2. If handle is NULL, return 0 (invalid track ID)\n3. Access the track ID table pointer from the Bink handle at offset 0x1f4 (500 decimal)\n4. Use the track index to access the track ID from the table (index * 4 byte stride)\n5. Return the track ID value\n\nParameters:\n- pBinkHandle (BinkHandle *): Pointer to Bink video file handle structure, must not be NULL\n- nTrackIndex (int): Zero-based index of the track to query\n\nReturns:\n- Track ID (int): Valid track identifier for the specified track index\n- 0: Invalid handle (NULL pointer) or track not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL handle pointer returns 0 immediately\n- Track index bounds checking is not performed by this function\n- Caller must ensure nTrackIndex is valid for the video file\n\nStructure Layout:\nBinkHandle Structure (partial):\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type    Description\n0x1f4   4     pTrackIdTable       int *   Pointer to array of track IDs\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1f4 (500 decimal): Offset to track ID table pointer in Bink handle\n- 0x4: Size of each track ID entry (4 bytes per int)\n- 0x0: Invalid track ID returned for error conditions",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
