      "name": "ClearMmxState",
      "signature": "void ClearMmxState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clear MMX Technology State\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute EMMS instruction to transition from MMX to floating-point state\n2. Clear all tag bits in FPU tag register to empty state  \n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function completes state transition and returns\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is critical for proper FPU/MMX state management\n- Must be called after MMX instructions before floating-point operations\n- Missing call can cause floating-point exceptions or incorrect results\n\nError Handling:\n- No error conditions possible - EMMS is atomic instruction\n- Always succeeds in clearing MMX state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
