      "name": "AlternativePixelHandler",
      "signature": "undefined AlternativePixelHandler(undefined4 param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Alternative pixel row handler for double-buffered color conversion processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current buffer pointers (g_pSrcBufferCurrent, g_pSrcBufferEnd)\n2. Swap to alternate processing buffers (g_pBufferBase, g_pBufferMidpoint)\n3. Call conversion function via g_nConversionRowStride with row parameter\n4. Calculate byte count from processed data (current - base)\n5. Copy processed base buffer to first saved destination (DWORD + byte copy)\n6. Copy processed base buffer to offset destination (saved + g_nInputRowBytes)\n7. Copy processed midpoint buffer to second saved destination\n8. Copy processed midpoint buffer to offset destination\n9. Update buffer pointers with new positions (original + byte count)\n\nParameters:\ndwRowParam - Row parameter passed to conversion function callback\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates global buffer pointers g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferEnd\n\nBuffer Layout:\ng_pBufferBase     - Start of primary processing buffer\ng_pBufferMidpoint - Start of secondary processing buffer\ng_nInputRowBytes  - Stride offset between row pairs in destination\n\nCopy Operations:\nUses REP MOVSD for DWORD-aligned bulk copy followed by REP MOVSB for remainder.\nFour copy operations total: base->saved1, base->saved1+stride, mid->saved2, mid->saved2+stride\n\nCalled By:\nConfigureColorProcessingPath - When alternative processing path selected (bit 1 set)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
