      "name": "ConfigureStateMachineDispatch",
      "signature": "void ConfigureStateMachineDispatch(uint dwStateLevel)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures state machine dispatch function pointers based on control register flags and level parameter\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read current state machine control register value into dwStatusRegister\n2. Check if bit 1 (0x02) is set in control register for flag mode operation\n3. If flag mode: Clear bit 1, store level shifted to bits 8-15, set paths 3&4 to CD10/CDD0, return\n4. Extract 6-bit counter mask from bits 2-7 into dwCounterMask\n5. Compare input level against current level stored in bits 8-15 of control register\n6. If level below current: Check if counter is zero for initial state or setup decrement state\n7. If level above or equal: Check if counter at maximum (0x3F) for reset or setup increment state\n8. Update control register with new counter value and state flags\n9. Set appropriate function pointer pairs for next execution phase\n\nParameters:\ndwStateLevel - uint - Target execution level or state index for state machine transition\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, operates through side effects on global state variables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If control register bit 1 set: Enters flag mode, bypasses normal state logic\n- Counter value 0: Sets initial state with paths 1&2 pointing to CD10/CDD0\n- Counter value 0x3F (63): Resets to state 1 with paths 1&2 pointing to CBB0/CC60\n- Level parameter determines transition direction (increment vs decrement)\n\nFlag Bits Reference:\n0x01 - State active flag\n0x02 - Flag mode enable (bypasses counter logic)\n0xFC - Counter value field (6 bits, values 0-63)\n0xFF00 - Level storage field (8 bits, shifted left 8)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3F (63) - Maximum counter value for 6-bit field\n0xFC - Mask for counter bits in control register\n0xFD - Inverse mask to clear bit 1 (flag mode)\n0x1000CBB0/CC60 - Function pointers for normal operation mode\n0x1000CD10/CDD0 - Function pointers for initial/flag mode operation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
