      "name": "ExpandPixelsWithPaletteLookup2x",
      "signature": "undefined ExpandPixelsWithPaletteLookup2x(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Expands palette-indexed pixels with 2x horizontal scaling.\n\nReads source bytes one at a time, uses each byte as an index into a\n32-bit color palette lookup table, and writes the resulting color value\ntwice to the destination buffer (achieving 2x horizontal expansion).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nPixelCount is zero, return immediately (no work to do)\n2. Loop nPixelCount times:\n   a. Read one byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent, advance pointer by 1 byte\n   b. Use the byte value as an index into g_anLookupTable to get 32-bit color\n   c. Write the color value to g_pSrcBufferCurrent[0] and g_pSrcBufferCurrent[1]\n   d. Advance g_pSrcBufferCurrent by 2 DWORDs (8 bytes)\n   e. Decrement counter and continue if not zero\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused: Unused parameter (reserved for callback compatibility)\n- nPixelCount: Number of source pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8): Pointer to source byte buffer (palette indices)\n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0): Pointer to destination DWORD buffer (expanded colors)\n- g_anLookupTable (0x1003674c): 256-entry palette lookup table (32-bit colors)\n\nNotes:\n- Each source byte produces 2 identical 32-bit pixels in destination\n- Naming convention: \"Dst/Src\" in globals appear swapped relative to actual data flow",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a56bb4787e4f4f8ad6e05b001d58f463838c604801b73f336a2c78944946b567",
