      "name": "CopyDoubledPixelsFromLookup",
      "signature": "undefined CopyDoubledPixelsFromLookup(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies indexed pixel values to two destination rows simultaneously.\n\nReads byte indices from g_pDstBufferCurrent, uses them to look up 32-bit pixel \nvalues from g_anLookupTable, and writes each pixel to both g_pSrcBufferCurrent \nand a parallel row offset by g_dwPixelStride. This effectively doubles pixel \nrows vertically for 2x scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if nPixelCount is zero\n2. For each pixel index:\n   a. Read byte index from source buffer, advance source pointer by 1 byte\n   b. Look up 32-bit pixel value using index into g_anLookupTable\n   c. Write pixel to primary destination (g_pSrcBufferCurrent)\n   d. Write same pixel to secondary row (g_pSrcBufferCurrent + g_dwPixelStride)\n   e. Advance destination pointer by 4 bytes (one DWORD)\n   f. Decrement counter, continue if non-zero\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused    - uint: Reserved/unused parameter (padding for alignment)\n  nPixelCount - int: Number of pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to source byte indices (incremented by 1 per pixel)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to destination pixel buffer (incremented by 4 per pixel)\n  g_anLookupTable     - 256-entry DWORD palette/lookup table for index-to-pixel conversion\n  g_dwPixelStride     - Byte offset to secondary row (typically scanline width)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:440f13f9b8fdf60bd48162bc2adcacd2080008ffc97360a02abdf10bdcedbce0",
