      "name": "ScalePixels2x",
      "signature": "undefined ScalePixels2x(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Scales indexed pixels to 2x size by duplicating each pixel into a 2x2 block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if pixel count is zero\n2. For each input pixel:\n   a. Read byte index from source buffer (g_pDstBufferCurrent)\n   b. Look up 32-bit color value from palette table (g_anLookupTable)\n   c. Write color to 4 adjacent pixels forming 2x2 block:\n      - Top-left:  g_pSrcBufferCurrent[0]\n      - Top-right: g_pSrcBufferCurrent[1]\n      - Bottom-left:  *(g_pSrcBufferCurrent + g_dwPixelStride)\n      - Bottom-right: *(g_pSrcBufferCurrent + g_dwPixelStride + 4)\n   d. Advance source pointer by 1 byte\n   e. Advance destination pointer by 8 bytes (2 pixels * 4 bytes)\n3. Decrement counter and loop until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*) - Unused parameter, passed but ignored\n  nPixelCount (int) - Number of source pixels to scale\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to current position in indexed source buffer (8-bit)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to current position in 32-bit destination buffer\n  g_anLookupTable - Palette lookup table converting 8-bit index to 32-bit color\n  g_dwPixelStride - Byte offset to next scanline in destination buffer\n\nNotes:\n  - Referenced only from function pointer table at 0x1002db84\n  - Part of pixel scaling/blitting subsystem\n  - Source reads 1 byte per pixel, destination writes 4 dwords (16 bytes) per source pixel",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
