      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbDoubledPixels",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbDoubledPixels(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV420 pixel data to RGB24, doubling each output pixel horizontally.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each input pixel in the count:\n   a. Fetch Y-to-Red index from U chroma lookup table\n   b. Compute Y-to-Green index as sum of U-to-green and V-to-blue lookups\n   c. Fetch V-to-Red index from V chroma lookup table\n   d. Read luminance (Y) byte from destination buffer, advance pointer\n   e. Use luminance to index into base lookup table for color component base addresses\n   f. Combine R, G, B components: (Red << 16) | (Green << 8) | Blue\n   g. Write the same RGB pixel to two consecutive destination positions (2x horizontal scaling)\n   h. Advance source buffer pointer by 2 DWORDs (8 bytes)\n2. Every 2 pixels (when dwPixelIndex is even), advance U and V chroma pointers\n   This implements 4:2:0 chroma subsampling where U/V are shared across 2 horizontal pixels\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index for chroma subsampling phase tracking\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert (loop count)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount * 8 bytes (2 DWORDs per pixel)\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes (1 luminance byte per pixel)\n  g_pChromaBufferU - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes (shared across 2 pixels)\n  g_pChromaBufferV - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes (shared across 2 pixels)\n  g_nYToRedIndex, g_nYToGreenIndex, g_nVToRedIndex - Temporary lookup indices\n\nColor Space:\n  YUV420 to RGB24 conversion using precomputed lookup tables for fast conversion.\n  Horizontal 2x scaling duplicates each RGB pixel for display upscaling.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
