      "name": "ConvertYUVToRGB24Pair",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToRGB24Pair(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color data to packed RGB24 format for two scanlines simultaneously.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pixel pair iteration:\n   a. Look up Y-to-Red index from U chroma buffer via g_adYToRedLookupTable\n   b. Calculate Y-to-Green index by combining U and V lookup tables\n   c. Look up V-to-Red index from V chroma buffer\n   d. Read luminance (Y) value and get base lookup pointer\n   e. Pack RGB components: (R << 16) | (G << 8) | B into 24-bit value\n   f. Write packed RGB to both current scanline and next scanline (pixel doubling)\n2. Advance chroma buffer pointers every other pixel (4:2:0 subsampling)\n3. Repeat until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  dwStartIndex - Starting pixel index for chroma buffer advancement tracking\n  dwPixelCount - Number of pixel pairs to process\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferEnd buffers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Chroma subsampling 4:2:0: U and V buffers advance every 2 pixels (when index is even)\n  Pixel doubling: Each RGB value written twice (horizontal 2x scaling)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Global lookup tables used for YUV to RGB conversion:\n  - g_adYToRedLookupTable: Y component to Red channel mapping\n  - g_adYToGreenLookupTable: Y component to Green channel base\n  - g_adUToBlueLookupTable: U chroma to Blue channel offset\n  - g_adVToRedLookupTable: V chroma to Red channel offset\n  - g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable: Base pointer for final RGB lookup",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a3b15d4ae44fa60bd40e63a134903685bf60a3add01ff247fb96ee3698bab4aa",
