      "name": "ConvertYUVToRGBPair",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToRGBPair(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space to RGB using lookup tables for video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pixel pair in the scanline:\n2. Read U/V chroma values from global chroma buffers\n3. Look up Y->Red, Y->Green, U->Blue, V->Red color indices\n4. For first pixel: read luminance (Y), combine color components via lookup tables\n5. Pack RGB as (V_red << 16 | Y_green << 8 | Y_red) into 32-bit pixel\n6. Write pixel to current line and duplicate to next line (pixel doubling)\n7. Repeat steps 4-6 for second pixel using alternate luminance buffer\n8. Every 2 pixels, advance U/V chroma pointers (4:2:0 subsampling)\n9. Loop until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount - Number of pixel pairs to convert (loop counter)\ndwStartOffset - Starting offset for pixel index tracking\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written to g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferEnd\n\nSpecial Cases:\nChroma subsampling: U/V buffers advance every 2 pixels (4:2:0 format)\nPixel doubling: Each converted pixel written to two scanlines via g_dwPixelStride\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x8 - Bit shift for packing RGB components\n0x4 - DWORD size for lookup table indexing\n0x1 - Mask for even/odd pixel detection (chroma advance)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
