      "name": "ConvertYUVToRGBDoubled",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToRGBDoubled(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:0 video data to RGB pixels with 2x2 pixel doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pixel in nPixelCount:\n2. Fetch Y-to-Red index from chroma U lookup table\n3. Compute Y-to-Green index by adding U-to-Blue contribution\n4. Fetch V-to-Red index from chroma V lookup table\n5. Read luminance byte and advance source pointer by 1\n6. Use luminance as base index into RGB component tables\n7. Pack RGB: (Red << 16) | (Green << 8) | Blue\n8. Write pixel to 2x2 block (current, +1, +stride, +stride+1)\n9. Advance destination pointer by 8 bytes (2 dwords)\n10. Every 2nd pixel, advance U and V chroma pointers\n\nParameters:\ndwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index for chroma subsampling alignment\nnPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert (loop count)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global buffer pointers as side effect\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount * 2 dwords\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\ng_pChromaBufferU - Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\ng_pChromaBufferV - Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x8 - Bit shift for RGB channel packing\n0x1 - Mask for odd/even pixel check\n0x4 - Bytes per pixel in stride offset",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:777da272cacd0ab6d25eccf57ba66279c8d948df028d4112b88f01ee3b403566",
