      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbDoubled",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbDoubled(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space to RGB with 2x2 pixel doubling for video scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each source pixel, look up Y, U, V chroma components from global buffers\n2. Calculate color indices using lookup tables for Y-to-Red, Y-to-Green, U-to-Blue, V-to-Red\n3. Pack RGB components into 32-bit pixel value: (R << 16) | (G << 8) | B\n4. Write pixel to 2x2 block in destination (current pixel, next horizontal, next row, next row+1)\n5. Advance U and V chroma pointers every 2 pixels (4:2:0 subsampling)\n6. Process both current and end buffer positions per iteration\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelCount - Number of pixels to process in the conversion loop\n  dwPixelOffset - Starting pixel offset for chroma subsampling alignment\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferEnd destinations\n\nGlobal State:\n  g_pChromaBufferU/V - Source chroma (U/V) plane pointers, advanced every 2 pixels\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent/End - Source luminance (Y) plane pointers\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent/End - Destination RGB buffer pointers\n  g_dwPixelStride - Row stride for 2x scaling vertical offset\n  g_adYToRedLookupTable - Y component to red channel lookup\n  g_adYToGreenLookupTable - Y component to green channel lookup  \n  g_adUToBlueLookupTable - U component to blue channel lookup\n  g_adVToRedLookupTable - V component to red channel lookup\n  g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable - Base luminance to RGB offset lookup\n\nColor Packing:\n  RGB packed as 0x00RRGGBB in little-endian 32-bit format\n  Bit shifts: Red << 16, Green << 8, Blue << 0",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1eb6c374c4f2994b50fadc857f0831702070e2a0c52c34713b778d794ce26653",
