      "name": "TranslateBufferViaLookupTable",
      "signature": "undefined TranslateBufferViaLookupTable(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Translates buffer entries using a lookup table.\n\nReads byte indices from the destination buffer, looks up corresponding\nvalues in g_anLookupTable, and writes results to the source buffer.\nBoth buffer pointers are global and auto-incremented.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If dwCount is zero, return immediately\n2. Loop dwCount times:\n   a. Read byte index from g_pDstBufferCurrent\n   b. Look up value in g_anLookupTable[index]\n   c. Write result to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n   d. Increment destination pointer by 1 byte\n   e. Increment source pointer by 4 bytes (DWORD)\n   f. Decrement counter and continue loop\n\nParameters:\n  dwReserved - uint - Reserved/unused parameter (ignored by function)\n  dwCount    - uint - Number of entries to translate from buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Incremented by 1 byte per iteration (0x100332e8)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Incremented by 4 bytes per iteration (0x100332e0)\n\nGlobals Read:\n  g_anLookupTable - 256-entry DWORD lookup table at 0x1003674c",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
