      "name": "TranslateDualBuffersThroughLookup",
      "signature": "int TranslateDualBuffersThroughLookup(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Translates bytes from dual source buffers through a lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop nIterationCount times\n2. For each iteration:\n   a. Read byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent, use as index into g_anLookupTable\n   b. Write lookup result (dword) to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n   c. Increment g_pDstBufferCurrent by 1 byte\n   d. Read byte from g_pDstBufferEnd, use as index into g_anLookupTable\n   e. Write lookup result (dword) to g_pSrcBufferEnd\n   f. Increment g_pDstBufferEnd by 1 byte\n   g. Advance both source pointers by 4 bytes (sizeof(uint))\n3. Return sum of nIterationCount + nBaseOffset\n\nParameters:\n  nIterationCount - Number of byte pairs to process through lookup table\n  nBaseOffset - Base offset value added to result\n\nReturns:\n  int - Sum of nIterationCount + nBaseOffset (total advancement)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Current position in first source byte stream\n  g_pDstBufferEnd (0x100332ec) - Current position in second source byte stream  \n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Current position in first destination dword stream\n  g_pSrcBufferEnd (0x100332e4) - Current position in second destination dword stream\n  g_anLookupTable (0x1003674c) - 256-entry lookup table for byte-to-dword translation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ef664b448381ac54234c42c62d21e4b542312dda46f5146645a882f42adfa746",
