      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbScanlinePixels",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbScanlinePixels(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space pixels to RGB24 format using lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through nPixelCount pixels starting at dwPixelIndex\n2. For each pixel:\n   a. Read U chroma value, look up Y-to-Red contribution index\n   b. Read U chroma for Y-to-Green index, add V chroma U-to-Blue contribution\n   c. Read V chroma, look up V-to-Red contribution index\n   d. Read luminance (Y) value from destination buffer, increment pointer\n   e. Use luminance to index into base lookup table\n   f. Combine R, G, B channels by shifting and OR-ing lookup results\n   g. Write packed RGB24 pixel to source buffer, advance pointer\n3. Every 2 pixels (when dwPixelIndex is even), advance U and V chroma pointers\n   (chroma subsampling - U/V shared between pixel pairs)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index (used for chroma subsampling alignment)\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nPixelCount is 0, function returns immediately\n  - Chroma pointers only advance on even pixel boundaries (4:2:2 subsampling)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  - g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount * 4 bytes\n  - g_pDstBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\n  - g_pChromaBufferU: Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\n  - g_pChromaBufferV: Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\n  - g_nYToRedIndex, g_nYToGreenIndex, g_nVToRedIndex: Scratch variables",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:fcb519bd30ff051cca9785a1621826aa0dae6e87a2ea6333e2d7df7262610310",
