      "comment": "Expands indexed 8-bit color values to 24-bit RGB with vertical line doubling.\n\nReads indexed bytes from source buffer, converts each to RGB16 via lookup table,\nthen writes as 24-bit RGB (3 bytes) to both the current scanline and the next\nscanline (offset by stride), effectively doubling the vertical resolution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exit early if pixel count is zero\n2. Loop for each pixel:\n   a. Read indexed byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent, increment pointer\n   b. Look up RGB16 color from g_anLookupTable using byte as index\n   c. Write RGB16 as 2 bytes + low byte as 3rd byte to current scanline\n   d. Write same 3 bytes to next scanline (current + stride)\n   e. Advance destination pointer by 3 bytes\n   f. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*): Unused parameter, reserved for interface compatibility\n  nPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (uint*): Source buffer pointer for indexed bytes (READ/WRITE)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (uint*): Destination buffer pointer for RGB24 (READ/WRITE)\n  g_anLookupTable (uint[]): Color lookup table, indexed by byte value (READ)\n  g_dwPixelStride (uint): Byte offset to next scanline for vertical doubling (READ)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero pixel count: Returns immediately without processing\n  - Vertical doubling: Same pixel written to current line and next line",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
