      "name": "ExpandIndexedColorPairs",
      "signature": "int ExpandIndexedColorPairs(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Expands indexed color bytes to RGB triplets using palette lookup table.\n\nReads indexed byte values from two input streams, looks up corresponding\n16-bit color values in a palette table at 0x1003674c, and writes expanded\n3-byte RGB values to both primary and secondary output buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to nPixelCount\n2. For each iteration:\n   a. Read byte from stream 1 at [0x100332e8], increment pointer\n   b. Look up 16-bit color in palette table (byte * 4 + 0x1003674c)\n   c. Write 3 bytes (word + low byte) to primary buffer [0x100332e0]\n   d. Write same 3 bytes to secondary buffer at offset [0x1003331c]\n   e. Repeat steps a-d for stream 2 ([0x100332ec] -> [0x100332e4])\n   f. Advance both destination pointers by 3 bytes\n   g. Decrement counter and loop if not zero\n3. Return nPixelCount + nOffset\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixel pairs to expand (loop iteration count)\n  nOffset - Value added to nPixelCount for return calculation\n\nReturns:\n  int - Sum of nPixelCount and nOffset (next buffer position)\n\nGlobal References:\n  0x100332e8 - Input stream 1 read pointer\n  0x100332ec - Input stream 2 read pointer\n  0x100332e0 - Output buffer 1 write pointer\n  0x100332e4 - Output buffer 2 write pointer\n  0x1003331c - Secondary buffer base offset\n  0x1003674c - Color palette lookup table (256 entries, 4 bytes each)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
