      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbWithVerticalDouble",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbWithVerticalDouble(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color data to RGB format with vertical pixel doubling.\n\nProcesses pixels using lookup tables for YUV to RGB color space conversion,\nwriting each pixel to two scanlines simultaneously for vertical scaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exit early if pixel count is zero\n2. For each pixel in the scanline:\n   a. Look up Y-to-Red index from U chroma channel\n   b. Calculate Y-to-Green index from U + U-to-Blue contribution\n   c. Look up V-to-Red index from V chroma channel\n   d. Read luminance (Y) value from destination buffer\n   e. Look up RGB base values from luminance lookup table\n   f. Write RGB triplet to current scanline (bytes 0-2, 3-5)\n   g. Write same RGB triplet to next scanline using stride offset\n   h. Advance source buffer by 6 bytes (two RGB pixels)\n   i. Every 2 pixels, advance U and V chroma pointers (4:2:2 subsampling)\n3. Continue until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index for chroma subsampling alignment\n  nPixelCount  - Number of pixels to process in this scanline\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pChromaBufferU       - Pointer to U chroma plane data\n  g_pChromaBufferV       - Pointer to V chroma plane data\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent    - Pointer to luminance (Y) source data\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent    - Pointer to RGB destination buffer\n  g_dwPixelStride        - Byte offset to next scanline for vertical doubling\n  g_adYToRedLookupTable  - Y component to Red channel lookup table\n  g_adYToGreenLookupTable- Y component to Green channel lookup table\n  g_adUToBlueLookupTable - U component to Blue channel lookup table\n  g_adVToRedLookupTable  - V component to Red channel lookup table\n  g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable - Luminance to RGB base value lookup\n\nNotes:\n  - Uses 4:2:2 chroma subsampling (U/V advance every 2 pixels)\n  - Writes 6 bytes per iteration (2 RGB pixels) to each scanline\n  - Vertical doubling duplicates each row to the next scanline via stride",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
