      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbWithChromaSubsampling",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbWithChromaSubsampling(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV pixel data to RGB format using lookup tables with 4:2:2 chroma subsampling.\n\nThis function processes pixels from YUV color space to RGB, reading luminance (Y) values\nfrom g_pDstBufferCurrent and chroma (U/V) values from g_pChromaBufferU/V. The conversion\nuses precomputed lookup tables for color component calculation and writes 6 bytes of RGB\ndata per 2 input pixels (handling the 4:2:2 chroma subsampling where U/V are shared).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if nPixelCount is zero\n2. For each pixel in nPixelCount:\n   a. Read U/V chroma values and compute lookup table indices\n   b. Store color component indices in g_nYToRedIndex, g_nYToGreenIndex, g_nVToRedIndex\n   c. Read luminance byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent, advance pointer\n   d. Look up base luminance in g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable\n   e. Write 6 bytes of RGB data to g_pSrcBufferCurrent using indexed lookup\n   f. Advance g_pSrcBufferCurrent by 6 bytes\n   g. On even pixel indices (dwPixelIndex & 1 == 0), advance U/V chroma pointers\n3. Return after all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index, used for chroma subsampling phase (odd/even toggle)\n  nPixelCount  - Number of pixels to convert, loop terminates when decremented to zero\n\nReturns:\n  void - Output written directly to buffer at g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n\nGlobal State:\n  Reads:  g_pChromaBufferU, g_pChromaBufferV, g_pDstBufferCurrent (Y plane)\n  Reads:  g_adYToRedLookupTable, g_adYToGreenLookupTable, g_adUToBlueLookupTable\n  Reads:  g_adVToRedLookupTable, g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable\n  Writes: g_pSrcBufferCurrent, g_nYToRedIndex, g_nYToGreenIndex, g_nVToRedIndex\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  6 - Bytes written per 2 pixels (3 RGB bytes x 2)\n  1 - Bitmask for odd/even pixel check (dwPixelIndex & 1)\n  4 - Stride multiplier for lookup table indexing",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
