      "name": "ConvertYuv420ToRgb24PixelPair",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuv420ToRgb24PixelPair(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:0 pixel pairs to RGB24 format for two scanlines simultaneously.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load chroma values from U and V buffers\n2. Compute color component indices using YUV-to-RGB lookup tables:\n   - Y-to-Red index from U channel\n   - Y-to-Green index from U + U-to-Blue from V \n   - V-to-Red index from V channel\n3. For current scanline:\n   a. Read luminance byte and look up base table entry\n   b. Write 6 RGB bytes (2 pixels) using color indices\n4. For second scanline (end buffer):\n   a. Read luminance byte and look up base table entry\n   b. Write 6 RGB bytes (2 pixels) using same color indices\n5. Advance destination pointers by 6 bytes each\n6. Every 2nd iteration, advance chroma U/V pointers (4:2:0 subsampling)\n7. Decrement pixel counter and loop until zero\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixel pairs to process (loop counter)\n  dwColumnOffset - Column offset for chroma subsampling phase tracking\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written to global destination buffer pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Chroma pointers advance only on even iterations (4:2:0 horizontal subsampling)\n  - Two scanlines processed per call for vertical chroma sharing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  6 - Bytes per 2 RGB pixels (2 * 3 bytes/pixel)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1731ff33a8a602a21c2e2b1b44d9792bec5b2ba66ec0774278998abb8b8ec7ce",
