      "name": "ConvertYUVToRGB24",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToRGB24(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:2 encoded video data to 24-bit RGB pixel format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pixel in nPixelCount:\n   a. Read Y (luminance) value from destination buffer\n   b. Compute color channel indices from chroma (U/V) lookup tables\n   c. Write R, G, B bytes to source buffer for current row\n   d. Write R, G, B bytes to source buffer for next row (using stride)\n   e. Advance source pointer by 3 bytes (RGB triplet)\n2. Every 2 pixels (when dwPixelOffset is even):\n   a. Advance U chroma pointer by 1\n   b. Advance V chroma pointer by 1\n   (Implements 4:2:2 chroma subsampling - U/V shared by 2 horizontal pixels)\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelOffset - Starting pixel offset used to track even/odd pixel position\n                  for chroma subsampling. Determines when to advance U/V pointers.\n  nPixelCount   - Number of pixels to process in this conversion pass\n\nReturns:\n  void - Results written directly to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n\nGlobal State Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent      - Source luminance (Y) data pointer, advanced each pixel\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent      - Destination RGB buffer pointer, advanced by 3 each pixel\n  g_pChromaBufferU         - Chroma U plane pointer, advanced every 2 pixels\n  g_pChromaBufferV         - Chroma V plane pointer, advanced every 2 pixels\n  g_dwPixelStride          - Row stride for writing second row pixels\n  g_adYToRedLookupTable    - Y component to red index lookup (256 entries)\n  g_adYToGreenLookupTable  - Y component to green index lookup (256 entries)\n  g_adUToBlueLookupTable   - U component contribution to green (256 entries)\n  g_adVToRedLookupTable    - V component to red index lookup (256 entries)\n  g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable - Base luminance to RGB lookup (256 entries)\n\nColor Space Conversion:\n  Uses precomputed lookup tables for efficient YUV to RGB conversion.\n  Standard YUV 4:2:2 format where chroma (U/V) is horizontally subsampled 2:1.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ae6a2c9d94107e2eabd2f09afdb34c154e00b81816fb992785f3217d80655d57",
