      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgb24DoubledScanline",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgb24DoubledScanline(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:0 pixel data to RGB24 format with vertical line doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each pixel in the scanline (nPixelCount iterations):\n   a. Calculate color component indices from chroma (U/V) lookup tables\n   b. Fetch luminance (Y) value from destination buffer, advance pointer\n   c. Use luminance index to look up RGB values from combined lookup table\n   d. Write RGB triplet to current scanline position\n   e. Write duplicate RGB triplet to position + stride (vertical double)\n   f. Repeat steps b-e for second Y value (g_pDstBufferEnd buffer)\n   g. Advance both RGB output pointers by 3 bytes (one RGB24 pixel)\n   h. Every 2nd pixel, advance U and V chroma pointers (4:2:0 subsampling)\n2. Loop until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n   nPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert in this scanline\n   dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index (used for chroma subsampling alignment)\n\nReturns:\n   void - Results written to global buffer pointers\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n   g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount * 3 bytes\n   g_pSrcBufferEnd - Advanced by nPixelCount * 3 bytes  \n   g_pDstBufferCurrent - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\n   g_pDstBufferEnd - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\n   g_pChromaBufferU - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes\n   g_pChromaBufferV - Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes\n   g_nYToRedIndex, g_nYToGreenIndex, g_nVToRedIndex - Intermediate lookup indices\n\nLookup Tables Used:\n   g_adYToRedLookupTable[256] - Y to red component index\n   g_adYToGreenLookupTable[256] - Y to green component base\n   g_adUToBlueLookupTable[256] - U to blue/green adjustment\n   g_adVToRedLookupTable[256] - V to red component index\n   g_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable[256] - Y to base RGB lookup pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   Chroma subsampling: U/V buffers advance every 2 pixels (4:2:0 format)\n   Vertical doubling: Each output pixel is duplicated at +g_dwPixelStride offset",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
