      "name": "ConvertIndexedToRgb24",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertIndexedToRgb24(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts indexed color bytes to RGB24 format using a lookup table.\n\nReads byte values from g_pDstBufferCurrent, uses each as an index into \ng_anLookupTable to get a 24-bit RGB value, then writes the RGB triplet \nto g_pSrcBufferCurrent. Both buffer pointers are advanced accordingly.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nPixelCount is zero; if so, return immediately\n2. For each pixel:\n   a. Read one byte from source buffer (g_pDstBufferCurrent)\n   b. Increment source pointer by 1 byte\n   c. Look up RGB value using byte as index into g_anLookupTable\n   d. Write low 16 bits as short to destination (R, G bytes)\n   e. Write byte 2 of RGB value to destination+2 (B byte)\n   f. Increment destination pointer by 3 bytes\n   g. Decrement pixel count and loop if non-zero\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*): Unused context pointer (reserved for compatibility)\n  nPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to convert\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount * 3 bytes\n\nNote: The lookup table at g_anLookupTable contains 256 entries of 4 bytes \neach, where only the lower 3 bytes (RGB24) are used per entry.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2721d9a1acf6d008bea616818a7bebda45766cb11c0867f78496ac52b5dcf6cd",
