      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbScanline",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbScanline(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space pixels to RGB using precomputed lookup tables.\nProcesses a scanline of video data by reading YUV values from separate\nchroma planes and converting to packed RGB output using indexed lookups.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pixel count is zero and exit early if so\n2. For each pixel in the scanline loop:\n3.   Read Y luminance value from U chroma buffer\n4.   Look up red component index from Y-to-Red lookup table\n5.   Read Y luminance value from V chroma buffer\n6.   Combine green index from Y-to-Green and U-to-Blue tables\n7.   Look up blue component index from V-to-Red table\n8.   Read compressed index byte from destination buffer\n9.   Use luminance base lookup to resolve RGB component bytes\n10.  Write 3 RGB bytes (R, G, B) to output buffer\n11.  Advance output buffer pointer by 3 bytes\n12.  Every 2 pixels, advance both U and V chroma pointers\n\nParameters:\ndwPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert in this scanline (uint)\nnStartIndex - Starting pixel index used for odd/even chroma tracking (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; writes directly to g_pSrcBufferCurrent buffer\n\nGlobals Used:\ng_pChromaBufferU - Pointer to U chroma plane source data\ng_pChromaBufferV - Pointer to V chroma plane source data\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to compressed index byte source\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to RGB output destination buffer\ng_adYToRedLookupTable - Y luminance to red component lookup (256 entries)\ng_adYToGreenLookupTable - Y luminance to green component lookup (256 entries)\ng_adUToBlueLookupTable - U chroma to blue component lookup (256 entries)\ng_adVToRedLookupTable - V chroma to red component lookup (256 entries)\ng_adLuminanceBaseLookupTable - Base luminance conversion table (256 entries)\ng_nYToRedIndex - Cached red component index from current Y value\ng_nYToGreenIndex - Cached green component index from current Y value\ng_nVToRedIndex - Cached blue component index from current V value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
