      "name": "DoublePixelsVerticalWithLookup",
      "signature": "undefined DoublePixelsVerticalWithLookup(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Doubles pixels vertically using a color lookup table for 16-bit output.\n\nReads indexed color bytes from g_pDstBufferCurrent, converts each through \ng_adLookupTable to get 16-bit color values, then writes the same pixel to\ntwo consecutive scanlines in g_pSrcBufferCurrent (current line and line at \ng_dwPixelStride offset), effectively doubling the vertical resolution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nPixelCount is zero; if so, return immediately\n2. Loop for each pixel:\n   a. Read one byte from source buffer (indexed color)\n   b. Advance source pointer by 1 byte\n   c. Look up 16-bit color value in g_adLookupTable using byte as index\n   d. Write 16-bit color to current scanline position\n   e. Write same 16-bit color to position offset by g_dwPixelStride (next scanline)\n   f. Advance destination pointer by 2 bytes (16-bit pixel)\n   g. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused     - void* : Unused parameter (reserved for function pointer compatibility)\n  nPixelCount - int   : Number of pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Source buffer with indexed color bytes (READ, incremented by 1 per pixel)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Destination buffer for 16-bit pixels (WRITE, incremented by 2 per pixel)\n  g_adLookupTable     - Color lookup table indexed by byte value, returns 16-bit color\n  g_dwPixelStride     - Byte offset between scanlines for vertical doubling\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If nPixelCount is 0, function returns immediately without processing",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c19b77b86f4a3aabe7de54887584318c6f70e8667cf5f120e17918bc74c73053",
