      "name": "ConvertAndDoublePixelRows",
      "signature": "int ConvertAndDoublePixelRows(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts indexed pixel bytes to 16-bit color values with vertical doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop nPixelCount times processing pixels from two source buffers\n2. For each pixel in first source buffer (g_pDstBufferCurrent):\n   a. Read byte index, advance pointer by 1\n   b. Look up 16-bit color in g_adLookupTable\n   c. Write color to current row (g_pSrcBufferCurrent)\n   d. Write same color to next row (current + g_dwPixelStride) for vertical doubling\n3. Repeat for second source buffer (g_pDstBufferEnd -> g_pSrcBufferEnd)\n4. Advance destination pointers by 2 bytes (16-bit color)\n5. Return total bytes consumed from source buffers\n\nParameters:\n- nPixelCount: Number of pixels to process per row\n- nSecondRowOffset: Offset for second row data (added to return value)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Sum of nPixelCount + nSecondRowOffset (total source bytes consumed)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4cfa8c2ad8faed7a0dee9a7014724deb2035fee095ba54439223a0deefb4e6b1",
