      "name": "ExpandBufferIndicesWithLookup",
      "signature": "int ExpandBufferIndicesWithLookup(int nIterationCount, int nReturnOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Expands byte indices from destination buffers to word values in source buffers using lookup table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to nIterationCount\n2. Read byte index from g_pDstBufferCurrent, advance pointer by 1 byte\n3. Look up ushort value at g_awLookupTable[byteIndex] \n4. Store ushort value at g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferCurrent+2\n5. Read byte index from g_pDstBufferEnd, advance pointer by 1 byte\n6. Look up ushort value at g_awLookupTable[byteIndex]\n7. Store ushort value at g_pSrcBufferEnd and g_pSrcBufferEnd+2  \n8. Advance g_pSrcBufferCurrent and g_pSrcBufferEnd by 4 bytes each\n9. Decrement loop counter and repeat until counter reaches zero\n10. Return nIterationCount + nReturnOffset\n\nParameters:\n  nIterationCount (int): Number of buffer pairs to process in the expansion loop\n  nReturnOffset (int): Offset value added to iteration count for return calculation\n\nReturns:\n  int: Sum of nIterationCount + nReturnOffset (typically used as total processed count)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x4 (4): Advance amount for source buffer pointers (2 ushort values = 4 bytes)\n  0x2 (2): Offset for second ushort storage location  \n  0x1 (1): Advance amount for destination buffer pointers (1 byte per index)\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal buffer pointers accessed:\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent: Current position in destination buffer (reads byte indices)\n- g_pDstBufferEnd: End position in destination buffer (reads byte indices)  \n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Current position in source buffer (writes ushort pairs)\n- g_pSrcBufferEnd: End position in source buffer (writes ushort pairs)\n- g_awLookupTable[256]: Lookup table mapping byte indices to ushort values",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
