      "name": "DoublePixels16Bit",
      "signature": "undefined DoublePixels16Bit(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Doubles pixels for 16-bit color video rendering by writing a 2x2 block for each source pixel.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pixel count is zero, return early if so\n2. For each pixel in the count:\n   a. Read byte index from global source stream pointer (g_pSourceStream at 0x100332e8)\n   b. Look up 16-bit color from palette table at 0x1003634c using index * 4\n   c. Write color to current destination (g_pDestRow at 0x100332e0)\n   d. Write color to destination + 2 (horizontal neighbor)\n   e. Write color to secondary row buffer (g_pSecondaryRow at 0x1003331c + dest offset)\n   f. Write color to secondary row + 2 (horizontal neighbor on next row)\n   g. Advance destination pointer by 4 bytes (2 pixels worth)\n   h. Advance source stream by 1 byte\n3. Loop until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused     - void* : Unused parameter (possibly for callback signature compatibility)\n  nPixelCount - int   : Number of pixels to process/double\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal Data Accessed:\n  0x100332e8 (g_pSourceStream)  - Byte stream containing palette indices\n  0x100332e0 (g_pDestRow)       - Destination buffer pointer (current row)\n  0x1003331c (g_pSecondaryRow)  - Secondary row offset for vertical doubling\n  0x1003634c (palette table)    - 16-bit color lookup table indexed by source byte * 4\n\nNotes:\n  - This is a 2x2 pixel doubling routine for scaling Bink video frames\n  - Each source byte index maps to a 16-bit color via palette lookup\n  - Output is 4 pixels (2x2 block) per input byte",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:191369953db4cced7c931d2441ad21b0600b95d63bfd7cfaf0cf15b7e8558010",
