      "name": "ProcessPixelBlockUpscale2x",
      "signature": "int ProcessPixelBlockUpscale2x(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes pixel blocks with 2x upscaling using palette lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop nPixelCount times\n2. For each iteration, read byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent source buffer\n3. Look up 16-bit color value in g_adLookupTable palette\n4. Write color to 2x2 pixel block at g_pSrcBufferCurrent (4 pixels total)\n5. Repeat for g_pDstBufferEnd -> g_pSrcBufferEnd buffer pair\n6. Advance all buffer pointers by 4 bytes (2 pixels width)\n7. Return sum of nPixelCount + nPitch\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of source pixels to process per row\n  nPitch - Row pitch value added to return\n\nReturns:\n  Sum of nPixelCount + nPitch (used for row offset calculation)\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to current source byte stream\n  g_pDstBufferEnd - Pointer to alternate source byte stream\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to current destination pixel buffer\n  g_pSrcBufferEnd - Pointer to alternate destination pixel buffer\n  g_adLookupTable - 256-entry palette lookup table (byte -> 16-bit color)\n  g_dwPixelStride - Bytes per row in destination buffer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ef541b363977cd939dab6c55a5a35803f665fb9baefefc7a049b6a6ac0de356c",
