      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgb16WithChromaSubsampling",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgb16WithChromaSubsampling(int param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:0 subsampled video data to RGB16 (RGB565) pixel format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read U and V chroma samples from global chroma buffer pointers\n2. Compute color indices using Y-to-red, Y-to-green, and V-to-red lookup tables\n3. For each pixel pair in the scanline:\n   a. Read Y luminance sample from destination buffer\n   b. Convert Y value to base coefficient via lookup table\n   c. Combine red, green, blue shifted values via OR into RGB16 pixel\n   d. Write RGB16 pixel to both current and next scanline (vertical doubling)\n4. Advance chroma pointers every 2nd pixel (4:2:0 horizontal subsampling)\n5. Loop until nPixelCount pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixel pairs to convert (loop counter, decremented)\n  dwStartIndex - Starting pixel index within scanline (used for odd/even chroma timing)\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pChromaBufferU/V - Pointers to U and V chroma plane data\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent/End - Y luminance source buffer pointers\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent/End - RGB16 destination buffer pointers\n  g_dwPixelStride - Offset to next scanline for vertical pixel doubling\n  g_ad*LookupTable - Color space conversion lookup tables (YUV to RGB)\n  g_an*ShiftedLookup - Pre-shifted RGB component lookup tables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1 - Mask for odd/even pixel index (chroma subsampling timing)\n  0x2 - RGB16 pixel size (2 bytes per pixel)\n\nNotes:\n  - Implements YUV 4:2:0 to RGB565 conversion with vertical line doubling\n  - Chroma values are shared between 2 horizontal pixels (4:2:0 subsampling)\n  - Each output pixel is written twice (current line and stride offset line)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8f92300506da6099f21751b591312ac9c018780e7c518d05b5403cf53264070f",
