      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgb16Doubled",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgb16Doubled(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space pixels to 16-bit RGB format with horizontal pixel doubling.\n\nProcesses pixels from a YUV source buffer and writes doubled RGB16 output pixels.\nEach output pixel is written twice (duplicated horizontally) for 2x horizontal scaling.\nThe U/V chroma planes are subsampled - only advanced every 2 pixels (4:2:2 subsampling).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pixel count is zero, return immediately (nothing to process)\n2. For each pixel in the source buffer:\n   a. Read U chroma value and compute Y-to-Red index from lookup table\n   b. Combine Y-to-Green and U-to-Blue lookup values for green index\n   c. Read V chroma value and compute V-to-Red index from lookup table\n   d. Read current Y luminance byte and advance luminance pointer\n   e. Get base coefficient from Y value using YUV base table\n   f. Combine shifted R, G, B lookup values via OR to form RGB16 pixel\n   g. Write RGB16 value to current output position\n   h. Write same RGB16 value to next output position (horizontal doubling)\n   i. Advance output pointer by 4 bytes (2 pixels x 2 bytes each)\n   j. Increment pixel counter; if now even, advance U and V chroma pointers\n3. Decrement remaining pixel count and loop until complete\n\nParameters:\n  dwStartIndex - Starting pixel index for processing (used for chroma phase tracking)\n  nPixelCount  - Number of source pixels to convert (loop iteration count)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; results written directly to g_pSrcBufferCurrent output buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nPixelCount is 0 or negative, function returns immediately\n  - Chroma pointers only advance on even pixel boundaries (4:2:2 subsampling)\n  - Output is doubled: each source pixel produces 2 identical RGB16 pixels\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent  - Advanced by nPixelCount * 4 bytes (2 RGB16 pixels per source)\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent  - Advanced by nPixelCount bytes (1 Y value per source pixel)\n  g_pChromaBufferU     - Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\n  g_pChromaBufferV     - Advanced by nPixelCount / 2 bytes\n  g_nYToRedIndex       - Set to final Y-to-Red lookup index\n  g_nYToGreenIndex     - Set to final Y-to-Green combined index\n  g_nVToRedIndex       - Set to final V-to-Red lookup index\n\nLookup Tables Used:\n  g_adYToRedLookupTable    - Y component to red channel contribution\n  g_adYToGreenLookupTable  - Y component to green channel contribution\n  g_adUToBlueLookupTable   - U chroma to blue channel contribution  \n  g_adVToRedLookupTable    - V chroma to red channel contribution\n  g_anYuvBaseCoefficients  - Base offset coefficients indexed by Y value\n  g_adBlueShiftedLookup    - Pre-shifted blue values for RGB16 packing\n  g_adGreenShiftedLookup   - Pre-shifted green values for RGB16 packing\n  g_adRedShiftedLookup     - Pre-shifted red values for RGB16 packing",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
