      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgb16Scaled2x2",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgb16Scaled2x2(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV pixel data to RGB16 format with 2x2 upscaling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pixel count is zero, return immediately if so\n2. For each pixel in the count:\n   a. Calculate Y-to-Red component from U chroma channel lookup\n   b. Calculate Y-to-Green component from U chroma + U-to-Blue from V chroma\n   c. Calculate V-to-Red component from V chroma channel lookup\n   d. Read luminance value from destination buffer and advance pointer\n   e. Look up luminance index in conversion table\n   f. Combine RGB components using lookup tables to produce RGB16 pixel\n   g. Write the same RGB16 pixel to a 2x2 block (4 pixels total):\n      - Top-left and top-right at current position\n      - Bottom-left and bottom-right at position + stride\n   h. Advance source buffer pointer\n   i. Increment pixel index; on even indices, advance U and V chroma pointers\n   j. Decrement count and loop until zero\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index (used for chroma subsampling alignment)\n  nPixelCount - Number of input pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nPixelCount is 0, function returns immediately\n  - Chroma buffers (U/V) advance only on even pixel indices (4:2:0 subsampling)\n  - Each input pixel produces a 2x2 block of identical RGB16 output pixels\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  - g_pDstBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount bytes\n  - g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Advanced by nPixelCount * 4 bytes (2x2 block)\n  - g_pChromaBufferU/V: Advanced by nPixelCount/2 bytes\n  - g_dwYToRedComponent, g_dwYToGreenComponent, g_dwVToRedComponent: Temp storage",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:eb6d8a79f229c70dbf2d530956d88e8524ea6654bcbc5f4fecae8650a8e4293f",
