      "name": "ExpandBytesToWordsWithLookup",
      "signature": "undefined ExpandBytesToWordsWithLookup(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Expands bytes to 16-bit words using a lookup table for color/palette conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if byte count is zero; if so, return immediately\n2. Loop for each byte to process:\n   a. Read one byte from source buffer (g_pDstBufferCurrent)\n   b. Advance source pointer by 1 byte\n   c. Use byte value as index into g_adLookupTable to get 16-bit value\n   d. Write 16-bit value to destination buffer (g_pSrcBufferCurrent)\n   e. Advance destination pointer by 2 bytes\n   f. Decrement counter and repeat until zero\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused     - void* : Unused parameter (reserved for callback compatibility)\n  nByteCount  - int   : Number of bytes to expand (each byte becomes one 16-bit word)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nByteCount is 0, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Source bytes are masked to 8-bit range for table indexing\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to source byte stream (advanced by 1 per iteration)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to destination word stream (advanced by 2 per iteration)\n  g_adLookupTable     - 256-entry lookup table mapping bytes to 16-bit values",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ae768f2d988268ca26db3bec62ddf8d59a9ceed4bc2f1c1b62571d6325dcbeb8",
