      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgb16",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgb16(uint param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV 4:2:0 subsampled pixels to 16-bit RGB format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exit early if pixel count is zero\n2. For each pixel in the count:\n   a. Look up Y-to-Red index from U chroma channel\n   b. Calculate Y-to-Green index by combining U and V lookups\n   c. Look up V-to-Red index from V chroma channel  \n   d. Read luminance (Y) value from destination buffer\n   e. Get base YUV coefficient from luminance lookup table\n   f. Combine R, G, B components using shifted lookup tables\n   g. Write 16-bit RGB pixel to source buffer\n   h. Advance chroma pointers every 2 pixels (4:2:0 subsampling)\n3. Decrement count and loop until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  dwPixelIndex - Starting pixel index, used to track chroma subsampling phase\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If nPixelCount is 0, function returns immediately\n  - Chroma buffers (U/V) advance every 2 pixels due to 4:2:0 subsampling\n  - Output is 16-bit RGB (RGB565 or similar format)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1 - Mask for odd/even pixel check (chroma subsampling)\n  0x2 - Output pixel stride (16-bit = 2 bytes per pixel)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
