      "name": "ScalePixelsWithPaletteLookup",
      "signature": "undefined ScalePixelsWithPaletteLookup(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Scales pixels using palette lookup and writes to dual buffers.\n\nReads palette indices from source buffer, looks up 16-bit RGB values from \na 256-entry palette table, and writes the scaled pixel data to both primary\nand secondary destination buffers. Each pixel produces 6 bytes of output \n(RGB565 written twice for 2x vertical scaling).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if nPixelCount is zero\n2. For each pixel:\n   a. Read byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent (palette index)\n   b. Increment source pointer\n   c. Look up RGB565 color from g_anLookupTable[index]\n   d. Create doubled value: color | (color << 8)\n   e. Write 6 bytes to g_pSrcBufferCurrent (DWORD + WORD)\n   f. Write 6 bytes to secondary buffer at g_dwPixelStride offset\n   g. Advance destination pointer by 6 bytes\n3. Continue until all pixels processed\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused      - void* : Unused parameter (reserved for API compatibility)\n  nPixelCount  - int   : Number of pixels to process\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Pointer to source palette index buffer (read)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Pointer to primary destination buffer (write)\n  g_anLookupTable     - 256-entry RGB565 palette lookup table\n  g_dwPixelStride     - Offset to secondary buffer for double-buffering",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:08b9759ae1f4da1cee21487a3ee6bdbf9c15ef172620ad9eb0decad483b79367",
