      "name": "UpscalePixels2x2FromPalette",
      "signature": "int UpscalePixels2x2FromPalette(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Upscales 8-bit palette-indexed pixels to 16-bit color with 2x2 pixel doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read two 8-bit palette indices from source (current and end buffers)\n2. Convert each byte to packed 16-bit color: (index << 16) | index | 0x80008000\n3. Write each converted pixel twice horizontally (2 DWORDs = 4 pixels)\n4. Write same pixels to next scanline using g_dwPixelStride offset\n5. Advance source pointers by 2 bytes, dest pointers by 8 bytes (2 DWORDs)\n6. Repeat until nPixelCount pixels processed (decrements by 2 per iteration)\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to process (must be even, processed in pairs)\n  nReturnOffset - Value added to nPixelCount for return value\n\nReturns:\n  nPixelCount + nReturnOffset (total offset for caller's position tracking)\n\nPixel Format:\n  Input: 8-bit palette index (1 byte per pixel)\n  Output: 16-bit color with alpha (0x8000XXXX where XX = palette index)\n  The 0x8000 high bit in each 16-bit half-word sets the alpha/opaque flag\n\nMemory Layout:\n  Processes two separate buffer pairs simultaneously:\n  - g_pDstBufferCurrent/g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Forward buffer pair\n  - g_pDstBufferEnd/g_pSrcBufferEnd: Backward/end buffer pair\n  Each pixel is duplicated into a 2x2 block for upscaling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2840881b045d5df5906c6e29dee07caa8731b74104f7a946e25c3f5aaa5d1dff",
