      "name": "ExpandPixels8To16WithAlpha",
      "signature": "undefined ExpandPixels8To16WithAlpha(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Expands 8-bit indexed pixels to 16-bit ARGB1555 format with alpha bit set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwPixelCount >= 2 (minimum 2 pixels required for processing)\n2. Calculate loop iterations as dwPixelCount / 2 (process 2 pixels per iteration)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Read first 8-bit pixel from g_pDstBufferCurrent\n   b. Expand to 16-bit: (pixel << 16) | pixel | 0x80008000 (duplicates grayscale with alpha)\n   c. Write to g_pSrcBufferCurrent[0]\n   d. Read second 8-bit pixel from g_pDstBufferCurrent + 1\n   e. Expand similarly and write to g_pSrcBufferCurrent[1]\n   f. Advance source pointer by 2 bytes, destination by 8 bytes\n4. Return when all pixel pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused   [Stack+0x4] - Unused parameter (callback signature compatibility)\n  dwPixelCount [Stack+0x8] - Number of pixels to expand (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x80008000 - Sets bit 15 (alpha=1) in both 16-bit pixels packed into a DWORD\n  0x10       - Shift amount for packing two 16-bit pixels into DWORD\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwPixelCount < 2, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Processes pairs of pixels; odd pixel counts will skip the last pixel\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Source 8-bit pixel buffer pointer\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Destination 16-bit pixel buffer pointer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:dbd47426c9b0616cdd19645606d299c173cd016bd288695cca271b6265a0c611",
