      "name": "DuplicatePixelRowWithAlpha",
      "signature": "undefined DuplicatePixelRowWithAlpha(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Duplicates a row of indexed pixels to two scanlines with alpha flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pixel count is at least 2, return early if not\n2. Calculate pair count as dwPixelCount / 2\n3. For each pair:\n   a. Read 2 bytes from source buffer (low and high palette indices)\n   b. Combine into 32-bit value: (highByte << 16) | lowByte | 0x80008000\n   c. Write combined pixel to current destination scanline\n   d. Write same pixel to next scanline (via stride offset)\n   e. Advance source pointer by 2 bytes\n   f. Advance destination pointer by 4 bytes (one DWORD)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*): Unused parameter, likely reserved for callback signature\n  dwPixelCount (uint): Number of source pixels to process (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x80008000: Alpha mask for two packed ARGB1555 pixels (bit 15 set for each)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if dwPixelCount < 2\n  - Processes pixels in pairs, so odd pixel counts lose the last pixel\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent: Source palette index buffer pointer (reads 2 bytes per iteration)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Destination ARGB pixel buffer pointer (writes 4 bytes per iteration)\n  g_dwPixelStride: Byte offset to next scanline for vertical doubling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:df8b9c9defee2e8b619632c4ee624c3db092f5d8cb943af18e1d32a87d98ed76",
