      "name": "ConvertYUVToPackedYUYV",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYUVToPackedYUYV(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts planar YUV data to packed YUYV (YUY2) format.\n\nReads Y samples from g_pDstBufferCurrent, U samples from g_pChromaBufferU,\nand V samples from g_pChromaBufferV, then packs them into YUYV format\n(4 bytes per 2 pixels: Y0 U Y1 V) written to g_pSrcBufferCurrent.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate number of pixel pairs to process (dwWidth / 2)\n2. For each pixel pair:\n   a. Read Y0 from g_pDstBufferCurrent[0]\n   b. Read Y1 from g_pDstBufferCurrent[1]\n   c. Read U from g_pChromaBufferU (shared between pair)\n   d. Read V from g_pChromaBufferV (shared between pair)\n   e. Pack first DWORD: Y0 | (U << 8) | (Y0 << 16) | (V << 24)\n   f. Pack second DWORD: Y1 | (U << 8) | (Y1 << 16) | (V << 24)\n   g. Write 8 bytes (2 DWORDs) to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n   h. Advance all buffer pointers\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*): Unused parameter, likely reserved for context\n  dwWidth (uint): Width in pixels (must be >= 2, processed in pairs)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwWidth < 2, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Width is processed in pairs, so odd widths lose the last pixel\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  - g_pDstBufferCurrent: Advanced by dwWidth bytes\n  - g_pChromaBufferU: Advanced by dwWidth/2 bytes\n  - g_pChromaBufferV: Advanced by dwWidth/2 bytes\n  - g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Advanced by dwWidth*4 bytes (2 DWORDs per pair)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1b77a954c024971f47281b5d70409bc9544d12226cff6383f07e95027e7325fb",
