      "name": "ProcessChromaToRgbConversion",
      "signature": "int ProcessChromaToRgbConversion(int nPixelCount, int nBaseOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts YUV422 chroma data to RGB format by processing pixel pairs from separate U/V/Y buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter from nPixelCount (process pairs, so decrement by 2)\n2. Read chroma components: load V, U, Y bytes from separate global buffers\n3. Pack chroma data using CONCAT operations into 3-byte YUV value (uChromaPackedYUV)\n4. Advance chroma buffer pointers (V and U buffers) by 1 byte each\n5. Write packed YUV data to current source buffer position\n6. Read next Y component byte from destination buffer (pbYComponent)\n7. Create chroma mask (uChromaMask) by masking packed data with 0xff00ff and shifting left 8\n8. Advance destination buffer pointer by 2 bytes\n9. Combine Y component with chroma mask: (Y << 16) | mask | Y, write to source buffer + 4\n10. Repeat steps 6-9 for end buffer: read Y from destination end buffer\n11. Write combined data to source end buffer position\n12. Advance all buffer pointers: source buffers +8 bytes, destination buffers +2 bytes\n13. Decrement loop counter by 2, continue if counter > 0\n14. Return sum of nPixelCount + nBaseOffset\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to process (decremented by 2 each iteration)\nnBaseOffset (int): Base offset value added to final return calculation\n\nReturns:\nint: Sum of original pixel count and base offset (nPixelCount + nBaseOffset)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLoop processes pixel pairs (decrements by 2) - ensure nPixelCount is even\nGlobal buffer pointers are advanced during processing - affects subsequent calls\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xff00ff (16711935): Chroma component mask - isolates U and V channels\n0x8 (8): Buffer advancement stride - 2 pixels * 4 bytes per RGB pixel\n0x10 (16): Left shift amount for Y component positioning in RGB data\n0x2 (2): Loop decrement - processes 2 pixels per iteration",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d0194b740e0a7d2683427bdc64a07eb42f053483ad07d0030b04c760f09b4e1c",
