      "name": "PackYuvToYuyvDualScanlines",
      "signature": "undefined PackYuvToYuyvDualScanlines(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Packs planar YUV components into YUYV (packed 4:2:2) format for dual scanlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exit early if width < 2 (no pixel pairs to process)\n2. Calculate iteration count as width / 2 (processing 2 pixels per iteration)\n3. For each pixel pair:\n   a. Read V component byte from g_pChromaBufferV\n   b. Read U component byte from g_pChromaBufferU  \n   c. Read 2 Y (luma) bytes from g_pDstBufferCurrent\n   d. Pack into YUYV format: Y0 | U << 8 | Y1 << 16 | V << 24\n   e. Write packed DWORD to g_pSrcBufferCurrent\n   f. Write same DWORD to secondary buffer at pixel stride offset\n   g. Advance all buffer pointers\n4. Continue until all pixel pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (void*) - Unused parameter, likely for API compatibility\n  dwWidth (dword) - Width in pixels of scanline to process (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nGlobal Buffer Pointers:\n  g_pChromaBufferV (0x100332f4) - V (Cr) chroma plane pointer, advances by 1 per iteration\n  g_pChromaBufferU (0x100332f0) - U (Cb) chroma plane pointer, advances by 1 per iteration\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Y (luma) plane pointer, advances by 2 per iteration\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Output YUYV buffer pointer, advances by 4 per iteration\n  g_dwPixelStride (0x1003331c) - Stride offset for secondary scanline write\n\nPacked YUYV Format (little-endian DWORD):\n  Bits 0-7:   Y0 (first luma sample)\n  Bits 8-15:  U  (Cb chroma, shared between Y0 and Y1)\n  Bits 16-23: Y1 (second luma sample)\n  Bits 24-31: V  (Cr chroma, shared between Y0 and Y1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Width < 2: Function returns immediately (no work done)\n  - Dual output: Same packed data written to both primary and secondary buffers",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:07c003c8b16561658c1bb2bd3ae2198d571b0ffcffdd3b0d9eaee9504b215478",
