      "name": "ConvertPalette8ToARGB32x2",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertPalette8ToARGB32x2(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts 8-bit palette pixel data to 32-bit ARGB format with scanline duplication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate loop count as half the width (processes 2 pixels per iteration)\n2. For each iteration:\n   a. Read two consecutive 8-bit values from source buffer\n   b. Expand each byte to ARGB format: (byte << 16 | byte) << 8 | 0x800080\n      - Creates grayscale RGB (R=G=B=byte) with alpha=0x80\n   c. Write both ARGB values to destination buffer\n   d. Duplicate to second scanline at g_dwPixelStride offset\n   e. Advance source pointer by 2 bytes, destination by 8 bytes\n3. Loop until all pixel pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n- pContext: Unused context pointer (for API consistency with other converters)\n- dwWidth: Width in pixels to process\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x800080: Alpha channel mask (sets A=0x80 for 50% opacity)\n- Pixel format: 0xAARRGGBB where R=G=B for grayscale\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent: Source 8-bit palette data pointer\n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Destination 32-bit ARGB buffer pointer\n- g_dwPixelStride: Scanline stride for second row duplication",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:04f23afcc369bb571838adbca1838a2b5b747f69af7b851241f2ae78f496cb6f",
