      "name": "ConvertGrayscaleToYUV422Doubled",
      "signature": "int ConvertGrayscaleToYUV422Doubled(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts 8-bit grayscale pixel data to YUV422 format with 2x2 pixel doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read 2 grayscale bytes from source buffer (g_pDstBufferCurrent)\n2. Pack each Y value into YUV422: (Y << 16 | Y) << 8 | 0x800080\n   - Creates YUYV quad with neutral chroma (U=V=128)\n3. Write 8 bytes (2 doubled pixels) to current scanline (g_pSrcBufferCurrent)\n4. Write same 8 bytes to next scanline (offset by g_dwPixelStride)\n5. Repeat for second buffer pair (g_pDstBufferEnd/g_pSrcBufferEnd)\n6. Advance all pointers and loop until nPixelCount exhausted\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of source pixels to process (decremented by 2 per iteration)\n  nReturnAccumulator - Value added to nPixelCount for return value\n\nReturns:\n  nReturnAccumulator + nPixelCount (combined pixel count)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x800080 - Neutral UV values (U=128, V=128) for grayscale-to-YUV conversion\n  0x8 (EBP) - Destination stride increment (8 bytes = 2 YUYV pixels)\n\nNotes:\n  - Function referenced from data table at 0x1002dfa8\n  - Uses global buffer pointers for blit operation\n  - Implements 2x horizontal and 2x vertical pixel doubling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:13c7c3c9573eb69daf5e2f5347e2fa785ae3b835421b264a0800c2e117d6eb73",
