      "name": "ProcessPixelBufferWithAlpha",
      "signature": "int ProcessPixelBufferWithAlpha(int nPixelCount, int nAdditionalValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes pixel buffer pairs by applying alpha channel blending with color expansion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pixel counter from nPixelCount parameter\n2. Loop while pixel pairs remain (counter > 0):\n   3. Decrement counter by 2 (processing pixel pairs)\n   4. Read first byte from destination buffer current position\n   5. Expand byte to 16-bit by duplication (byte << 16 | byte)\n   6. Shift left 8 bits and OR with alpha constant 0x800080\n   7. Store processed 32-bit value to source buffer current position\n   8. Advance destination buffer pointer by 1 byte, read next byte\n   9. Advance destination buffer pointer by 2 total (skip processed pair)\n  10. Process second byte with same expansion and alpha blending\n  11. Store to source buffer current position + 1\n  12. Repeat steps 4-11 for destination end buffer to source end buffer\n  13. Advance source buffer pointers by 8 bytes (2 32-bit values)\n  14. Continue loop until all pixel pairs processed\n15. Return sum of input parameters\n\nParameters:\nnPixelCount (int): Number of pixels to process (must be even for pair processing)\nnAdditionalValue (int): Additional value added to return result\n\nReturns:\nint: Sum of nPixelCount + nAdditionalValue (processed pixel count confirmation)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x800080 - Alpha channel constant for color blending (RGB: 128,0,128 with alpha 128)\n0x10 - 16-bit shift for byte duplication in color expansion\n0x8 - 8-bit shift for final color positioning\n-2 - Pixel pair decrement (processes 2 pixels per iteration)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9adff6323942b78e0cb2af25e40cb389e17df5b0e84095879dcebbf1a4e390b9",
