      "name": "ConvertScanline16To32WithDouble",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertScanline16To32WithDouble(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts a scanline from 16-bit to 32-bit ARGB format with vertical doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if width is at least 2 pixels, exit early if not\n2. Calculate loop count as width / 2 (processing 2 source bytes per iteration)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Read 2 bytes from source buffer (16-bit pixel)\n   b. Convert to 32-bit: (highByte << 16 | lowByte) << 8 | 0x800080\n   c. Write 32-bit pixel to destination buffer\n   d. Write same pixel to stride-offset location (vertical doubling)\n   e. Advance source pointer by 2 bytes\n   f. Advance destination pointer by 4 bytes\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused - Unused parameter, reserved for callback signature compatibility\n  dwWidth  - Width of scanline in pixels\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Width < 2: Early exit, no processing performed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x800080 - Alpha mask ORed into pixel, sets bits 7 and 23 for alpha channels\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (100332e8) - Current position in 16-bit source buffer\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (100332e0) - Current position in 32-bit destination buffer\n  g_dwPixelStride     (1003331c) - Byte offset to next scanline for doubling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
