      "name": "ConvertBytePairsToArgbDoubled",
      "signature": "int ConvertBytePairsToArgbDoubled(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts byte pairs from two source buffers to ARGB pixels with vertical doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop processes 2 bytes per iteration from each source buffer\n2. Read low byte and high byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent, advance by 2\n3. Pack bytes into ARGB format: (highByte << 16 | lowByte) << 8 | 0x800080\n4. Write packed pixel to g_pSrcBufferCurrent and stride-offset position (vertical double)\n5. Repeat same process for second buffer pair (g_pDstBufferEnd -> g_pSrcBufferEnd)\n6. Advance destination pointers by 4 bytes (one DWORD)\n7. Continue until nRemainingPixels <= 0\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to process (decremented by 2 each iteration)\n  nStrideOffset - Offset added to return value (used for buffer advancement tracking)\n\nReturns:\n  nPixelCount + nStrideOffset - Combined pixel and stride offset for caller tracking\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x800080 - Alpha mask applied to packed pixel (sets alpha bits in ARGB format)\n  0x10 - Shift for high byte positioning in 32-bit pixel\n  0x8 - Final shift for byte alignment in ARGB packing\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Current position in first source byte buffer\n  g_pDstBufferEnd (0x100332ec) - Current position in second source byte buffer\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Current position in first destination pixel buffer\n  g_pSrcBufferEnd (0x100332e4) - Current position in second destination pixel buffer\n  g_dwPixelStride (0x1003331c) - Scanline stride for vertical pixel doubling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:51b237080c4af38a566d1f29fa419c39ee1e7c76ad0f2efa65a04a2bd756157c",
