      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbaWithVerticalDouble",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertYuvToRgbaWithVerticalDouble(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts YUV planar data to packed RGBA pixels with vertical line doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pixel count is valid (at least 2 pixels required)\n2. Calculate loop iterations as dwPixelCount / 2 (processing 2 pixels per iteration)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Read Y values from destination buffer (2 bytes: Y0, Y1)\n   b. Read U value from chroma U buffer (1 byte)\n   c. Read V value from chroma V buffer (1 byte)\n   d. Pack first pixel: [U, Y0, V, Y0] in little-endian UYVY format\n   e. Pack second pixel using Y1 with U/V from first pixel\n   f. Write both packed pixels to source buffer\n   g. Write same pixels to next scanline (vertical doubling via g_dwPixelStride offset)\n   h. Advance all buffer pointers\n\nParameters:\n  pReserved    - void*  - Unused parameter (reserved for callback signature compatibility)\n  dwPixelCount - uint   - Number of pixels to process (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If dwPixelCount < 2, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Pixels are processed in pairs due to YUV 4:2:2 chroma subsampling\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent  - Source Y plane data pointer (read, advanced by 2)\n  g_pChromaBufferU     - Chroma U plane pointer (read, advanced by 1)\n  g_pChromaBufferV     - Chroma V plane pointer (read, advanced by 1)\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent  - Output RGBA buffer pointer (written, advanced by 8 bytes)\n  g_dwPixelStride      - Scanline stride for vertical doubling\n\nPixel Packing Format (32-bit little-endian):\n  Pixel 1: byte[0]=U, byte[1]=Y0, byte[2]=V, byte[3]=Y0\n  Pixel 2: byte[0]=Y1, byte[1]=Y1, byte[2]=U&V masked, byte[3]=extracted\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xff00ff - Mask to extract alternating bytes for pixel reconstruction",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
