      "name": "ConvertYUVPlanarToYUYVPacked",
      "signature": "int ConvertYUVPlanarToYUYVPacked(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts YUV planar format to packed YUYV (YUY2) format for two scanlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop processes 2 pixels per iteration (nPixelCount decremented by 2)\n2. Read Y luma values from current destination buffer\n3. Read U and V chroma values from separate chroma planes\n4. Pack into YUYV format: Y0|U|Y1|V (4 bytes per 2 pixels)\n5. Write packed pixels to both current and end scanline buffers\n6. Advance all buffer pointers (Y by 2, U/V by 1)\n7. Continue until all pixels processed (nRemainingPixels <= 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nPixelCount - Number of pixels to convert (must be even)\n  nLineOffset - Offset value added to result for next line position\n\nReturns:\n  Sum of nPixelCount and nLineOffset for positioning next operation\n\nGlobal Buffer Pointers Used:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent  - Source Y luma buffer (current line)\n  g_pDstBufferEnd      - Source Y luma buffer (end/second line)\n  g_pChromaBufferU     - Source U chroma plane\n  g_pChromaBufferV     - Source V chroma plane\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent  - Destination YUYV buffer (current line)\n  g_pSrcBufferEnd      - Destination YUYV buffer (end/second line)\n\nYUYV Pixel Format:\n  Byte 0: Y0 (first luma sample)\n  Byte 1: U  (shared chroma)\n  Byte 2: Y1 (second luma sample)\n  Byte 3: V  (shared chroma)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xff00ff - Mask to extract U and V bytes from packed value\n  0x8      - Stride advance for destination buffers (2 YUYV pairs = 8 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:17aeb9e9305a2137e41f9488a7299845b44c33c8e7064538a0d508e2ed36d1ae",
