      "name": "ConvertPixels16To32WithAlpha",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertPixels16To32WithAlpha(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts 16-bit pixel data to 32-bit ARGB format with fixed alpha.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if dwPixelCount >= 2, return early if not\n2. Calculate iteration count as dwPixelCount / 2 (processes 2 bytes per iteration)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Read low byte from current source position\n   b. Read high byte from source position + 1\n   c. Combine bytes: (highByte << 16 | lowByte) << 8 | 0x800080\n   d. Write 32-bit result to destination buffer\n   e. Advance source by 2 bytes, destination by 4 bytes\n4. Loop until all pixel pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n- dwReserved: Unused parameter (reserved for future use or padding)\n- dwPixelCount: Number of bytes to process from source buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x800080: Alpha mask bits (sets bit 23 and bit 7 for ARGB format)\n- 0x10: Shift high byte to bits 16-23\n- 0x8: Final shift to position pixel data\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_pDstBufferCurrent: Source buffer pointer (despite misleading name)\n- g_pSrcBufferCurrent: Destination buffer pointer (despite misleading name)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
