      "name": "ConvertPixelRowTo32BitARGB",
      "signature": "int ConvertPixelRowTo32BitARGB(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts 16-bit pixel data to 32-bit ARGB format for two scanlines simultaneously.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through pixel pairs (2 bytes per iteration) until row width exhausted\n2. For each pair from current scanline buffer:\n   a. Read low byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent[0]\n   b. Read high byte from g_pDstBufferCurrent[1]\n   c. Combine into 16-bit value, shift left 8, OR with 0x800080 for alpha\n   d. Write 32-bit ARGB to g_pSrcBufferCurrent, advance pointer\n3. Repeat step 2 for end scanline buffer (g_pDstBufferEnd to g_pSrcBufferEnd)\n4. Return total bytes processed (nRowWidth + nRowOffset)\n\nParameters:\n  nRowWidth - Width of scanline in bytes (decremented by 2 per pixel pair)\n  nRowOffset - Additional offset added to return value\n\nReturns:\n  nRowWidth + nRowOffset (total bytes processed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x800080 - Alpha and component mask for ARGB conversion (sets alpha=0x80, R LSB=0x80)\n  0x10 - Shift for high byte placement (16 bits)\n  0x8 - Final shift for ARGB alignment\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_pDstBufferCurrent - Advanced by 2 bytes per pixel pair\n  g_pDstBufferEnd - Advanced by 2 bytes per pixel pair\n  g_pSrcBufferCurrent - Advanced by 4 bytes (1 uint) per pixel pair\n  g_pSrcBufferEnd - Advanced by 4 bytes (1 uint) per pixel pair",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2a7f61461f06bdcfa6022cd2e5b3e5f15e92bded568dd3b76c781b8d15ee3a10",
