      "name": "ProcessChromaUpsampling",
      "signature": "void ProcessChromaUpsampling(int nLineCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs chroma upsampling for video frame processing using MMX SIMD instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop for current buffer processing with line count multiplier\n2. Extract pixel data from destination buffer and chroma U/V channels\n3. Apply chroma bias subtraction using 64-bit MMX operations\n4. Perform left shift by 2 bits and high-precision multiply for scaling\n5. Extract individual 16-bit components from 64-bit MMX register\n6. Lookup color conversion coefficients from four transformation tables\n7. Add bias values and clamp using saturated arithmetic\n8. Apply right shifts with different amounts for R, G, B channels\n9. Left shift to position color channels in output format\n10. Combine RGB channels using bitwise OR operations\n11. Write final 64-bit pixel data to output buffer\n12. Repeat process for second buffer pass (end lines)\n\nParameters:\nnScanlineCount (int): Number of scanlines to process for chroma upsampling\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value - modifies global buffer pointers directly\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses MMX instruction set for parallel 16-bit arithmetic\n- Processes two separate buffer ranges: current and end\n- Global buffer pointers are updated during processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002dfc8: MMX bias constant for chroma processing (64-bit)\n0x1002dfb8: Chroma bias subtraction constant \n0x1002dfc0: High-precision multiply factor for scaling\n0x10034730: Color transformation table for red channel\n0x10034b30: Color transformation table for green channel (primary)\n0x10034f30: Color transformation table for green channel (secondary)\n0x10035330: Color transformation table for blue channel\n0x1003c7f0: Right shift amount for red channel positioning\n0x1003c7d8: Left shift amount for red channel final position\n0x1003c7f8: Right shift amount for green channel positioning\n0x1003c7e0: Left shift amount for green channel final position\n0x1003c800: Right shift amount for blue channel positioning\n0x1003c7e8: Left shift amount for blue channel final position\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Buffer Pointers (modified during execution):\nOffset | Size | Field Name           | Type      | Description\n-------|------|---------------------|-----------|----------------------------------\n0x0e0  | 4    | g_pSrcBufferCurrent | uint*     | Current source buffer pointer\n0x0e4  | 4    | g_pSrcBufferEnd     | uint*     | End source buffer pointer  \n0x0e8  | 4    | g_pDstBufferCurrent | uint*     | Current destination buffer\n0x0ec  | 4    | g_pDstBufferEnd     | uint*     | End destination buffer\n0x0f0  | 4    | g_pChromaBufferU    | uint*     | Chroma U component buffer\n0x0f4  | 4    | g_pChromaBufferV    | uint*     | Chroma V component buffer",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
