      "name": "ConvertYuv422ChromaToRgb",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuv422ChromaToRgb(int nWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV422 chroma data to RGB24 format using MMX SIMD instructions for optimized video processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate RGB output buffer stride (nWidth * 3 bytes per pixel)\n2. Load MMX constants for saturation arithmetic and color correction\n3. First processing loop (current buffer):\n   - Load 32-bit pixel data from source buffer and extract BGRA components\n   - Load U/V chroma values from separate chroma buffers\n   - Apply zero masking using PSUBUSW to prevent underflow\n   - Scale luminance by factor of 4 using PSLLW shift\n   - Apply chroma scaling factors via high-precision multiplication (PMULHW)\n   - Lookup red color components from 256-entry table indexed by chroma\n   - Lookup green color components from two tables (chroma and luminance)\n   - Lookup blue color components from single chroma table\n   - Add bias constants and clamp using saturated arithmetic (PADDSW/PSUBUSW)\n   - Pack 16-bit color values to 8-bit using PUNPCKLWD/PUNPCKHWD\n   - Interleave RGB channels into 24-bit pixels with bit shifting\n   - Store packed RGB triplets to output buffer advancing by 12 bytes per iteration\n4. Second processing loop (end buffer):\n   - Identical algorithm applied to second buffer set for double-buffering\n   - Uses separate buffer pointers for concurrent processing\n5. Update global buffer state pointers for next frame\n\nParameters:\nnWidth (int): Frame width in pixels for calculating buffer stride\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMMX register management requires 64-bit aligned data access\nColor lookup tables handle gamma correction and color space conversion\nSaturation arithmetic prevents color channel overflow/underflow\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002dfc8 - g_qwMmxRoundingConstant: Rounding bias for MMX arithmetic\n0x1002dfb8 - g_qwMmxZeroMask: Zero clipping mask (0x00FF00FF pattern)  \n0x1002dfc0 - g_qwMmxMultiplier: Chroma scaling multiplier\n0x10034730 - g_adRedLookupTable[256]: Red channel color correction table\n0x10034b30 - g_adGreenLookupTable[256]: Green channel base correction table\n0x10034f30 - g_adGreenChromaTable[256]: Green channel chroma correction table\n0x10035330 - g_adBlueLookupTable[256]: Blue channel color correction table\n\nError Handling:\nMMX saturation arithmetic (PADDSW/PSUBUSW) prevents overflow\nBuffer bounds checking via comparison with calculated end addresses\nNo explicit error returns - function assumes valid buffer setup\n\nPerformance Notes:\nProcesses 2 pixels per MMX iteration for 2x throughput\nParallel chroma processing reduces memory bandwidth requirements\nLookup tables provide O(1) gamma and color space correction",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
