      "comment": "Convert YUV color data to RGB using MMX SIMD instructions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate buffer end positions by adding nRows * 6 DWORDs to source pointers\n2. Process current buffer from g_pSrcBufferCurrent to calculated end position\n3. Extract Y, U, V components from source pixel data and chroma buffers\n4. Subtract zero mask (0x1002dfb8) from Y component and shift left by 2 bits\n5. Multiply by MMX multiplier constant (0x1002dfc0) using high-word multiply\n6. Extract signed word values from MMX register for 4 luminance deltas\n7. Look up red values using g_adRedLookupTable indexed by chroma V samples\n8. Look up green values using g_adGreenLookupTable and g_adGreenChromaTable\n9. Look up blue values using g_adBlueLookupTable indexed by chroma U samples\n10. Add rounding constant (0x1002dfc8) and subtract it back for rounding\n11. Pack RGB values into 32-bit pixels with proper bit positioning\n12. Store 6 packed RGB pixels to destination buffer and advance pointers\n13. Repeat until current buffer is fully processed\n14. Process end buffer from g_pSrcBufferEnd using identical conversion algorithm\n15. Update global chroma buffer pointers for next frame processing\n\nParameters:\nnRowCount (int): Number of rows to process in color conversion operation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function modifies global buffers in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses MMX instruction set for parallel processing of 4 pixels simultaneously\n- Requires aligned buffer access for MMX operations to prevent exceptions\n- Zero mask (0x1002dfb8) removes DC bias from luminance component\n- Multiplier constant (0x1002dfc0) scales luminance for proper dynamic range\n- Rounding constant (0x1002dfc8) ensures proper integer rounding in fixed-point math\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002dfb8 - MMX zero mask for Y component DC removal\n0x1002dfc0 - MMX multiplier constant for luminance scaling  \n0x1002dfc8 - MMX rounding constant for fixed-point arithmetic\n6 - DWORDs per processed pixel group (24 bytes RGB output per iteration)",
