      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbConversion",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvToRgbConversion(int nWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space data to RGB format using SIMD optimizations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize MMX/SSE registers and load RGB bias value from DAT_1002dfc8\n2. Setup buffer pointers for chroma U/V channels and destination RGB buffer\n3. Calculate new source buffer position based on width parameter\n4. Begin first processing loop for current buffer section:\n   a. Load destination pixel and chroma U/V bytes\n   b. Extract RGBA components using bit manipulation and CONCAT operations\n   c. Apply chroma subtraction with bias (PSUBUSW) and scale by 4 (PSLLW)\n   d. Perform high multiplication with conversion matrix (PMULHW)\n   e. Apply color space transformation using lookup tables:\n      - Red component: DAT_10034730 table indexed by chroma values\n      - Green component: DAT_10034f30 and DAT_10034b30 tables combined  \n      - Blue component: DAT_10035330 table indexed by chroma values\n   f. Add bias, clamp values, and pack into 64-bit RGB output\n   g. Store packed RGB data to destination buffer\n   h. Advance all buffer pointers by 2 pixels (8 bytes)\n5. Continue first loop until reaching source buffer end boundary\n6. Begin second processing loop for end buffer section using same algorithm\n7. Process remaining pixels with identical color conversion operations\n8. Complete when all end buffer data is processed\n\nParameters:\n\nnWidth (int): Width stride for buffer advancement calculation, determines how many pixels to advance source buffer pointer (nWidth * 4 bytes per advancement)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid - No return value, operates directly on global video buffers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nUses saturated arithmetic (PSUBUSW, PADDSW) to prevent color component overflow\nMMX/SSE operations process 4 pixels simultaneously for performance optimization\nChroma components are upsampled from byte to word precision during conversion\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x1002dfc8 - RGB bias value for color space conversion\n0x1002dfb8 - Chroma subtraction bias constant  \n0x1002dfc0 - Chroma scaling multiplication factor\n0x10034730 - Red component lookup table (256 entries)\n0x10034b30 - Green component lookup table 1 (256 entries)\n0x10034f30 - Green component lookup table 2 (256 entries) \n0x10035330 - Blue component lookup table (256 entries)\n\nGlobal Buffer References:\n\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Source buffer current position pointer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd - Source buffer end position pointer  \ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Destination buffer current position pointer\ng_pDstBufferEnd - Destination buffer end position pointer\ng_pChromaBufferU - Chroma U component buffer pointer\ng_pChromaBufferV - Chroma V component buffer pointer",
