      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbWithLookupTables",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuvToRgbWithLookupTables(int nPixelPairCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color data to RGB format using precomputed lookup tables for video processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save initial chroma buffer pointers (U and V channels) for later restoration\n2. Copy input pixel count parameter to local counter for second loop\n3. Read initial U and V chroma values from buffers and advance pointers\n4. Calculate color offsets using lookup tables: R offset from DAT_10033730[Y], B offset from DAT_10034330[V], G offset from DAT_10033f30[Y] + DAT_10033b30[V]\n5. Enter first processing loop for pixel pairs:\n   a. Read Y luminance value from destination buffer and advance pointer\n   b. Calculate luminance base offset using DAT_10038b60[Y]\n   c. Combine RGB components using CONCAT operations: R=(luminance+R_offset), G=(luminance+G_offset), B=(luminance+B_offset)\n   d. Store packed RGB value to source buffer and advance pointer\n   e. Process second pixel of pair with updated U/V values\n   f. Read two consecutive Y values and generate two more RGB pixels\n   g. Decrement pixel count and repeat until zero\n6. Restore chroma buffer pointers to saved positions\n7. Read final U and V values for second processing phase\n8. Enter second processing loop using g_pSrcBufferEnd and g_pDstBufferEnd pointers\n9. Process remaining pixels using same YUV to RGB conversion algorithm\n10. Restore chroma buffer pointers by decrementing to compensate for final reads\n\nParameters:\nnPixelPairCount - Number of pixel pairs to process (int)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction processes video data in two phases using separate buffer pointer sets (Current and End)\nChroma buffers (U/V) are shared between processing phases and require pointer restoration\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10033730 - Y to R conversion lookup table (256 entries * 4 bytes)\n0x10033b30 - U to B conversion lookup table (256 entries * 4 bytes)  \n0x10033f30 - Y to G conversion lookup table (256 entries * 4 bytes)\n0x10034330 - V to R conversion lookup table (256 entries * 4 bytes)\n0x10038b60 - Luminance base lookup table (256 entries * 4 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\nEach RGB pixel packed as 32-bit value: [unused:8][R:8][G:8][B:8]\nYUV data stored as separate Y, U, V channel buffers\nLookup tables provide precomputed coefficients for color space conversion",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
