      "name": "ProcessYuvToRgbConversionMmx",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvToRgbConversionMmx(int nStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes YUV to RGB color conversion using MMX SIMD instructions for optimized video rendering\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global chroma buffer pointers and advance source buffer position by stride\n2. Enter dual processing loop for current and end buffer ranges\n3. Extract packed ARGB pixels from destination buffer into MMX registers\n4. Load chroma U/V values from separate buffer channels\n5. Apply packed subtract-saturated subtraction to remove alpha channel\n6. Perform left-shift multiplication by 2 for color range expansion\n7. Apply high-order multiplication with MMX multiplier constant\n8. Compute red channel using chroma U lookup table with rounding constant\n9. Compute green channel using both chroma U and V lookup tables\n10. Compute blue channel using chroma V lookup table with rounding constant\n11. Apply color channel bit shifts using global shift configuration\n12. Combine RGB channels using bitwise OR operations\n13. Store final packed pixel data back to source buffer locations\n14. Advance all buffer pointers and repeat until buffer ranges complete\n\nParameters:\nnStride (int): Image row stride in pixels for buffer advancement calculations\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value, modifies global buffer contents in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nTwo identical processing loops handle current and end buffer ranges separately\nMMX rounding constant (g_qwMmxRoundingConstant) prevents color clipping artifacts\nColor lookup tables provide gamma correction and color space transformation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24): Bit shift for extracting alpha channel from packed ARGB\n0x10 (16): Bit shift for extracting red channel component\n0x08 (8): Bit shift for extracting green channel component\n0x02 (2): Left shift multiplier for color range expansion\n0x30 (48): High 16-bit extraction shift for MMX register manipulation\n0x20 (32): Mid-high extraction shift for packed pixel processing\n0xffffffff00ff00ff: MMX mask for packed byte channel extraction\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Buffer Pointers:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Current position in source image buffer\ng_pSrcBufferEnd - End position marker for source buffer\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Current position in destination buffer\ng_pDstBufferEnd - End position marker for destination buffer\ng_pChromaBufferU - U channel chroma component buffer\ng_pChromaBufferV - V channel chroma component buffer\n\nLookup Tables:\ng_adRedLookupTable - Red channel color transformation table\ng_adGreenLookupTable - Green channel base transformation table\ng_adGreenChromaTable - Green channel chroma adjustment table\ng_adBlueLookupTable - Blue channel color transformation table\n\nMMX Configuration:\ng_qwMmxZeroMask - Packed zero mask for MMX operations\ng_qwMmxMultiplier - High-precision multiplier constant\ng_qwMmxRoundingConstant - Rounding constant for accurate conversion\n_g_byRedRightShift/_g_byRedLeftShift - Red channel bit positioning\n_g_byGreenRightShift/_g_byGreenLeftShift - Green channel bit positioning\n_g_byBlueRightShift/_g_byBlueLeftShift - Blue channel bit positioning\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking performed - assumes valid buffer states\nMMX operations use saturated arithmetic to prevent overflow\nBuffer bounds checking relies on calling function validation",
