      "name": "ConvertYuvToRgbDualScanlines",
      "signature": "void ConvertYuvToRgbDualScanlines(int nScanlineCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts YUV color space data to RGB format processing two scanlines simultaneously using lookup tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Store initial chroma buffer pointers for second scanline processing\n2. Execute first scanline conversion loop:\n   a. Load U and V chroma values from input buffers, advance pointers\n   b. Load two Y luminance bytes from destination buffer, advance by 2 bytes  \n   c. Index into Y-to-component lookup tables using chroma values\n   d. Calculate RGB components using table lookups and bitwise OR\n   e. Store converted pixel pair to source buffer, advance by 2 positions\n   f. Repeat for second pixel pair in same scanline\n   g. Decrement scanline count and continue until first batch complete\n3. Execute second scanline conversion loop:\n   a. Reset chroma pointers to beginning of current scanline\n   b. Process pixel pairs identically to first loop but using end buffers\n   c. Advance scanline count for next iteration\n   d. Continue until all scanline pairs processed\n\nParameters:\n\nnScanlineCount (int): Number of scanline pairs to process\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nDual scanline processing optimizes memory bandwidth by reusing chroma data for vertically adjacent pixel pairs since YUV 4:2:0 format subsamples chroma components.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x4 (4): Stride for 32-bit DWORD lookups in color conversion tables",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
