      "name": "ProcessScaledPixelBlending",
      "signature": "void ProcessScaledPixelBlending(int nScaleFactor)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Optimized MMX-based pixel scaling and blending processor for image operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load MMX constants (zero mask, multiplier, rounding) from global memory\n2. Calculate source buffer end pointer using scale factor parameter\n3. First processing loop - Process source buffer current to calculated end:\n   a. Read two destination pixels from current buffer position\n   b. Unpack pixels to 16-bit components using PUNPCKLBW\n   c. Subtract zero mask values using PSUBUSW for proper range\n   d. Left shift components by 2 bits using PSLLW for precision\n   e. Multiply high words with MMX multiplier using PMULHW  \n   f. Apply rounding constant with saturated add/subtract (PADDSW/PSUBUSW)\n   g. Extract 16-bit components from 64-bit MMX registers\n   h. Multiply components with pack constant values\n   i. Store processed 64-bit results to source buffer (4 qwords)\n   j. Advance buffer pointers by 8 uint positions\n4. Second processing loop - Process source buffer end to final end:\n   a. Repeat same pixel processing operations for remaining data\n   b. Calculate final end pointer using source buffer end + scale factor\n   c. Store final buffer position back to global source end pointer\n\nParameters:\nnScaleFactor (int): Scaling multiplier for buffer size calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function modifies global buffer pointers and processes pixel data in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles two separate buffer regions (current->calculated end, end->final end)\n- MMX registers used for SIMD processing of multiple 16-bit components\n- Saturated arithmetic prevents overflow/underflow during processing\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4A854A854A854A85 - MMX multiplier constant for fixed-point scaling\n0x7F007F007F007F00 - MMX rounding constant for precision control  \n0x10001000100010 - MMX zero mask for component range adjustment\n0x1010100010101 - MMX pack constant for component reconstruction\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid global buffer pointers\nBuffer overflow protection relies on loop boundary conditions\nMMX state not explicitly saved/restored (assumes caller responsibility)",
