      "name": "BlendPixelsWithMmxMask",
      "signature": "void BlendPixelsWithMmxMask(int nPixelWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Blends pixel data using MMX SIMD instructions with a predefined blend mask.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit MMX blend mask from g_qwMmxBlendMask into MMX register\n2. Calculate end pointer for current buffer (g_pSrcBufferCurrent + nPixelWidth * 8 bytes)\n3. Process pixels in current buffer loop:\n   - Load destination pixel from g_pDstBufferCurrent\n   - Extract mask bytes: alpha (bits 24-31), red (bits 16-23), green (bits 8-15), blue (bits 0-7)\n   - Use PUNPCKLBW MMX instruction to unpack bytes and blend with destination pixel\n   - Store blended result as 64-bit value in source buffer\n   - Advance source buffer by 8 bytes, destination buffer by 4 bytes\n4. Update global buffer pointers to current position\n5. Calculate end pointer for end buffer (g_pSrcBufferEnd + nPixelWidth * 8 bytes)\n6. Process pixels in end buffer loop using identical MMX blending operation\n7. Update global end buffer pointers\n\nParameters:\nnPixelWidth (int): Width in pixels to process (determines loop iteration count)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x18 (24): Bit shift to extract alpha channel from 32-bit pixel\n0x10 (16): Bit shift to extract red channel from 32-bit pixel  \n0x08 (8): Bit shift to extract green channel from 32-bit pixel\n0x04 (4): Destination buffer stride (4 bytes per 32-bit pixel)\n0x08 (8): Source buffer stride (8 bytes per MMX-processed pixel)\n\nMMX Instruction Details:\nPUNPCKLBW: Unpack low-order bytes from MMX source and destination\n- Interleaves bytes from mask with pixel data for alpha blending\n- Operates on 8 bytes simultaneously for SIMD efficiency",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
