      "name": "ProcessFftRadix2Butterfly",
      "signature": "void ProcessFftRadix2Butterfly(int nComplexSamples, float * pfComplexArray, float * pfTwiddleTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs radix-2 FFT butterfly operations with twiddle factor multiplication on complex data array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process base 8-point complex butterfly computation (always executed)\n2. Apply twiddle factors from pfTwiddleTable[2] for initial 8-point transformation  \n3. If nComplexSamples > 16: Process 16-point butterfly with twiddle factors from pfTwiddleTable[4] and pfTwiddleTable[5]\n4. If nComplexSamples > 32: Enter loop to process remaining blocks of 16 complex samples\n5. For each loop iteration: Load four consecutive twiddle factors starting at offset 0x18\n6. Compute complex twiddle factor combinations using double angle formulas\n7. Apply butterfly operations with computed twiddle factors to 16-point block\n8. Advance pointers by 16 complex samples (64 bytes) and 16 twiddle factors (64 bytes)\n9. Decrement loop counter and repeat until all blocks processed\n\nParameters:\n- nComplexSamples (int): Number of complex samples in input array (must be power of 2, \u2265 8)\n- pfComplexArray (float*): Input/output array of interleaved real/imaginary values [real0, imag0, real1, imag1, ...]  \n- pfTwiddleTable (float*): Precomputed twiddle factor table indexed by transform size\n\nReturns:\nvoid (results written in-place to pfComplexArray)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- nComplexSamples \u2264 16: Processes only base 8-point and optional 16-point butterflies\n- nComplexSamples = 32: Processes 8-point, 16-point, and exactly one 16-point loop iteration\n- nComplexSamples > 32: Full recursive processing of all 16-point blocks\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x10 (16): Threshold for enabling 16-point butterfly processing\n- 0x20 (32): Threshold for enabling iterative loop processing  \n- 0x11 (17): Offset subtracted from nComplexSamples before bit shift for loop counter\n- 0x18 (24): Byte offset to first twiddle factors in iterative loop\n- 0x23 (35): Initial pfComplexArray offset for loop processing (points to 18th complex sample)\n\nComplex Number Layout:\nArray indices represent complex samples as [real_part, imaginary_part] pairs:\n- Index 0,1: Complex sample 0 (real, imaginary)\n- Index 2,3: Complex sample 1 (real, imaginary)  \n- Index 4,5: Complex sample 2 (real, imaginary)\n- etc.\n\nTwiddle Factor Usage:\n- pfTwiddleTable[2]: Applied to 8-point butterfly (offset +8)\n- pfTwiddleTable[4], pfTwiddleTable[5]: Applied to 16-point butterfly (offset +16, +20)\n- Loop twiddle factors: Four consecutive values loaded per iteration starting at offset 0x18\n\nError Handling:\nFunction assumes valid inputs - no bounds checking performed.\nUndefined behavior if nComplexSamples is not a power of 2 or < 8.\nUndefined behavior if pfComplexArray or pfTwiddleTable are NULL or invalid.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
