      "name": "ConfigureAudioSystem",
      "signature": "void ConfigureAudioSystem(int * pAudioConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures the audio system by calling a sequence of audio subsystem functions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call first audio function with handle from config (+0x44)\n2. Check audio mode type from config (+0x34) - compare with 0x10\n3. Calculate audio flags based on audio type (+0x38) and mode:\n   - If mode == 0x10: flags = ((audioType != 2) ? 3 : 1)\n   - If mode != 0x10: flags = ((audioType != 2) ? 2 : 0)\n4. Call second audio function with handle, flags, and boolean (mode == 0x10)\n5. Call third audio function with handle and parameter from +0x30\n6. Call audio volume callback with handle and volume from +0x58\n7. Call fifth audio function with handle and parameter from +0x5c\n8. Call sixth audio function with handle, 0, and parameter from +0x50\n9. Call final audio function with handle and callback address 0x1001aad0\n\nParameters:\npAudioConfig - Pointer to audio configuration structure containing:\n               +0x30: Audio parameter 1 (undefined4)\n               +0x34: Audio mode type (checked against 0x10)\n               +0x38: Audio type (checked against 0x2)\n               +0x44: Audio handle for all function calls\n               +0x50: Audio parameter 2\n               +0x58: Audio volume setting\n               +0x5c: Audio parameter 3\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 - Audio mode threshold for flag calculation\n0x2 - Audio type threshold for flag calculation\n0x30, 0x34, 0x38, 0x44, 0x50, 0x58, 0x5c - Structure field offsets\n0x1001aad0 - Callback function address passed to final audio call\n\nSpecial Cases:\nAudio flag calculation uses complex bitwise operations with SETNZ/DEC/AND/INC\nto convert boolean comparison results into specific flag values (0,1,2,3).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
