      "name": "SetAudioSystemState",
      "signature": "int SetAudioSystemState(int * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Controls the audio system enabled state for a Bink video instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check operation code (nOperation)\n2. If nOperation == 1 (Enable):\n   a. Check if audio is already enabled (pAudioConfig[10] != 0)\n   b. If not enabled, call ConfigureAudioSystem to initialize audio\n   c. Set enabled flag to 1\n3. If nOperation == 0 (Disable):\n   a. Check if audio is currently enabled (pAudioConfig[10] == 1)\n   b. If enabled, call audio cleanup function via g_pfnAudioInit with handle\n   c. Set enabled flag to 0\n4. If nOperation == other (Query):\n   a. Return current enabled state without modification\n5. Return the audio enabled state flag\n\nParameters:\npAudioConfig - Pointer to audio configuration structure containing:\n               +0x28 (index 10): Audio enabled state flag (0=disabled, 1=enabled)\n               +0x44 (index 17): Audio handle for cleanup function\nnOperation - Operation code:\n             0 = Disable audio (cleanup and set flag to 0)\n             1 = Enable audio (configure and set flag to 1)\n             Other = Query only (return current state)\n\nReturns:\nint - Current audio enabled state after operation (0 or 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Enable when already enabled: No-op, returns 1\n- Disable when already disabled: No-op, returns 0\n- Query operation: Returns state without side effects",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:83fa0c99c18a80018678d78b53af31f7553b13df4f13fb7607cf8b9576cd52ca",
