      "name": "BinkAudioCallbackHandler",
      "signature": "int BinkAudioCallbackHandler(BinkAudioContext * pBinkInstance, int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Handles Bink audio callback management based on operational mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nMode parameter equals 1 (shutdown mode)\n2. If nMode == 1: Call shutdown callback through DAT_1003c850 with audio handle from offset +0x44\n3. If nMode != 1: Call initialization callback through DAT_1003c868 with audio handle from offset +0x44\n4. For non-shutdown mode: Set flag at offset +0x54 to 1 (mark audio as initialized)\n5. Return nMode value as status indicator\n\nParameters:\npBinkInstance (BinkAudioContext *): Pointer to Bink audio context structure containing audio handles and state flags\nnMode (int): Audio callback mode - 1 for shutdown, other values for initialization\n\nReturns:\nint: Status code - returns 1 for shutdown mode, returns nMode value for initialization mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMode value 1 triggers shutdown path without setting initialization flag\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x44: Offset to audio handle within Bink audio context structure\n0x54: Offset to audio initialized flag within Bink audio context structure\n0x1: Shutdown mode constant (nMode comparison value)\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - relies on callback functions for error management",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
