      "name": "GetBinkBufferAlignment",
      "signature": "dword GetBinkBufferAlignment(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Returns the required buffer alignment for Bink video operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return the constant alignment value of 0x40 (64 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- 0x40 (64): Fixed buffer alignment requirement in bytes\n\nCalled By:\n- BinkOpenMiles: Used during Bink video initialization to determine memory alignment\n\nNotes:\n- The 64-byte alignment is a common requirement for media buffers to ensure\n  optimal memory access patterns and SIMD compatibility\n- This is a simple accessor returning a compile-time constant",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
