      "name": "RetryAudioBufferOperation",
      "signature": "void RetryAudioBufferOperation(AudioDeviceContext * pAudioContext, int nBufferMultiplier)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Retries audio buffer operations until successful completion or non-recoverable error.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter retry loop to attempt audio buffer operation\n2. Call audio device method through vtable at offset 0x2c with buffer parameters\n3. Pass calculated buffer size (dwBufferSize * nBufferMultiplier), buffer size, and output buffer pointers\n4. Check return value against device busy error code (0x88780096 = DSERR_BUFFERLOST)\n5. If device busy error detected, sleep for 10ms to allow device recovery\n6. Call device reset/recovery method through vtable at offset 0x50\n7. Jump back to retry loop start for another attempt\n8. If success or different error, exit retry loop and return\n\nParameters:\npAudioContext - Pointer to AudioDeviceContext structure containing:\n  lpVTable (offset 0x0) - Virtual function table pointer for device methods\n  dwBufferSize (offset 0xc) - Base buffer size in bytes for calculations\n  dwStatusBuffer1 (offset 0x38) - Status/state buffer 1 pointer\n  dwStatusBuffer2 (offset 0x3c) - Status/state buffer 2 pointer  \n  dwOutputBuffer1 (offset 0x40) - Output audio buffer 1 pointer\n  dwOutputBuffer2 (offset 0x44) - Output audio buffer 2 pointer\nnBufferMultiplier - Integer multiplier applied to base buffer size\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value, continues until operation succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x88780096 (decimal: -2005401450) - DSERR_BUFFERLOST or device busy error requiring retry\n0x2c (decimal: 44) - VTable offset for primary audio operation method\n0x50 (decimal: 80) - VTable offset for device reset/recovery method\n10 (0xa) - Sleep duration in milliseconds between retry attempts\n\nError Handling:\n- DSERR_BUFFERLOST (0x88780096): Sleep 10ms, reset device, retry operation\n- All other return codes: Exit immediately (success or non-recoverable error)\n- Infinite retry loop on persistent device busy conditions\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type    | Description\n0x00   | 4    | lpVTable        | void*   | Virtual function table pointer\n0x04   | 8    | dwReserved1-2   | uint    | Reserved fields\n0x0c   | 4    | dwBufferSize    | uint    | Base buffer size for calculations\n0x10   | 40   | dwReserved4-D   | uint    | Reserved/intermediate fields\n0x38   | 4    | dwStatusBuffer1 | uint    | Status buffer 1 pointer/handle\n0x3c   | 4    | dwStatusBuffer2 | uint    | Status buffer 2 pointer/handle\n0x40   | 4    | dwOutputBuffer1 | uint    | Output buffer 1 pointer/handle\n0x44   | 4    | dwOutputBuffer2 | uint    | Output buffer 2 pointer/handle",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:132b0efec00aaaa44f68f3e3bd1597d91e917c1099d786905068e1fbd9168048",
