      "name": "StartAudioPlaybackOperation",
      "signature": "int StartAudioPlaybackOperation(int nAudioContext, int * pnOutBufferHandle, int * pnOutBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initiates audio playback operation by validating device state and retrieving buffer information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate audio device context by checking buffer identifier at offset 0x6c is not -1\n2. Verify playback state is ready by checking status field at offset 0x78 equals 0\n3. If validation passes, call RetryAudioBufferOperation with device context + 0x3c and buffer ID\n4. Extract buffer handle from context offset 0x78 and store in output parameter\n5. Extract buffer size from context offset 0x74 and store in output parameter  \n6. Return 1 to indicate successful operation initiation\n7. If validation fails at any point, return 0 to indicate operation cannot proceed\n\nParameters:\n- nAudioContext: Integer handle/pointer to audio device context structure\n- pnOutBufferHandle: Pointer to receive current audio buffer handle/identifier\n- pnOutBufferSize: Pointer to receive current audio buffer size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Audio playback operation successfully initiated, buffer information populated\n- 0: Operation failed due to invalid device state or unavailable buffers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer ID -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) indicates no buffer allocated or device not initialized\n- Status field non-zero indicates playback already in progress or device busy\n- Output parameters remain unchanged if function returns 0\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x6c: Offset to buffer identifier field in audio context\n- 0x78: Offset to playback status field in audio context  \n- 0x74: Offset to buffer size field in audio context\n- 0x3c: Offset to AudioDeviceContext sub-structure within main context\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Invalid buffer identifier sentinel value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8debbe9151a733a1eaac4ab53e84c2f1c51a73dfeb4c647bd1dd1cba67db39f3",
