      "name": "audio_callback_6",
      "signature": "undefined4 audio_callback_6(int param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Handles Bink audio DirectSound callback messages for buffer state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check message code parameter against known values\n2. If nMessageCode == 1 (START):\n   a. Check if audio context state (+0x28) is already initialized\n   b. If not initialized, set buffer markers to -1 (+0x68, +0x6c)\n   c. Clear buffer positions (+0x60, +0x64) to 0\n   d. Set state flag to 1 (initialized)\n   e. Return current state value\n3. If nMessageCode == 0 (STOP):\n   a. Check if state flag is 1 (was initialized)\n   b. If so, call COM vtable method at +0x48 (Stop buffer)\n   c. Call COM vtable method at +0x34 (Release/cleanup)\n   d. Call ProcessAudioBufferWithWait for final processing\n   e. Set state flag to 0 (stopped)\n   f. Return state value\n4. If nMessageCode == other (STATUS QUERY):\n   a. Return current state flag value from +0x28\n\nParameters:\n- pAudioContext: Pointer to BinkAudioContext structure containing:\n  - +0x28: State flag (0=stopped, 1=playing)\n  - +0x3c: COM DirectSound buffer interface pointer\n  - +0x60: Buffer write position\n  - +0x64: Buffer read position  \n  - +0x68: Buffer start marker (-1 when uninitialized)\n  - +0x6c: Buffer end marker (-1 when uninitialized)\n- nMessageCode: Callback message type\n  - 0: Stop and cleanup audio\n  - 1: Initialize/start audio\n  - Other: Query current state\n\nReturns:\n- State flag value from audio context (+0x28)\n- 0: Audio stopped\n- 1: Audio playing/initialized\n\nCalled By:\n- BinkDirectSoundHandler (via function pointer reference at 0x1001c29f)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
