      "name": "StringCompareInsensitive",
      "signature": "int StringCompareInsensitive(char * lpszString1, char * lpszString2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Compares two strings case-insensitively using either simple ASCII or locale-aware conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global locale flag (g_dwLocaleFlags) to determine comparison method\n2. If locale flag is 0 (simple ASCII mode):\n   a. Initialize comparison with 0xFF sentinel value\n   b. Compare characters byte-by-byte until difference or null terminator\n   c. Convert both characters to uppercase using manual calculation:\n      - Subtract 0x41 (ASCII 'A'), check if < 0x1A (within A-Z range)\n      - Add 0x20 if lowercase letter to convert to uppercase\n      - Add 0x41 back to restore ASCII value\n   d. Compare converted characters and return difference\n3. If locale flag is non-zero (locale-aware mode):\n   a. Initialize packed character comparison with 0xFF sentinel\n   b. Compare characters byte-by-byte until difference or null terminator\n   c. Pack each character into 32-bit values using CONCAT31\n   d. Call FUN_1001dd1a (locale conversion function) for both characters\n   e. Compare converted byte values and return difference\n4. Return comparison result: negative if str1 < str2, 0 if equal, positive if str1 > str2\n\nParameters:\nlpszString1 (char*): First null-terminated string to compare\nlpszString2 (char*): Second null-terminated string to compare\n\nReturns:\nint: Comparison result following standard strcmp convention:\n     < 0 if lpszString1 lexicographically less than lpszString2\n     = 0 if strings are equal (case-insensitive)\n     > 0 if lpszString1 lexicographically greater than lpszString2\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf either string pointer is null, behavior is undefined\nEmpty strings (length 0) compare as equal\nNull terminator (0x00) acts as comparison sentinel\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x41 (65): ASCII value of 'A' - used as base for case conversion\n0x1A (26): Number of letters in alphabet - range check for A-Z\n0x20 (32): Difference between uppercase and lowercase ASCII values\n0xBF (191): Adjustment value in case conversion (256 - 65 = 191)\n0xFF (255): Initial sentinel value for comparison loops",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
