      "name": "ConvertFloat10ToDoubleAndCall",
      "signature": "void ConvertFloat10ToDoubleAndCall(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts two float10 values from FPU stack to double precision and passes to processing function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exchange ST0 and ST1 on FPU stack (FXCH)\n2. Store ST1 (originally ST0) as double to stack position [ESP]\n3. Store ST0 (originally ST1) as double to stack position [ESP + 0x8]\n4. Load high 32 bits of second double into EAX register\n5. Call FUN_1001d082 with four 32-bit parameters representing two doubles\n6. Clean up stack frame and return\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT in_ST0 (float10): First extended precision floating-point value on FPU stack\nIMPLICIT in_ST1 (float10): Second extended precision floating-point value on FPU stack\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function serves as FPU stack to double parameter conversion wrapper\n- Called from ProcessHuffmanDecodedSignals suggesting signal processing context\n- Uses SUB84 intrinsic to extract low 64 bits of double conversion\n- Shifts high bits to separate mantissa/exponent components\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x10 (16): Stack frame size for two double values (8 bytes each)\n0x8: Offset to second double on stack\n0xc: Offset to high 32 bits of second double (0x8 + 4)\n0x20 (32): Bit shift to extract high 32 bits from 64-bit value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
