      "name": "ProcessFloatControlFlags",
      "signature": "bool ProcessFloatControlFlags(uint dwFlags, double * pdValue, uint dwControlMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Process floating-point control flags and handle precision adjustments\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract control flags from dwFlags using bit mask 0x1F\n2. Check for precision exception conditions (flags & 0x8) with (dwControlMask & 0x1)\n3. If precision exception triggered, call exception handler and clear flag bit 3\n4. Check for underflow exception (flags & 0x4) with (dwControlMask & 0x4)\n5. If underflow detected, call exception handler and clear flag bit 2\n6. Check for overflow condition (flags & 0x1) with (dwControlMask & 0x8)\n7. If overflow detected, call exception handler and process rounding mode from dwControlMask bits 10-11:\n   - 0x000: Round toward zero (default)\n   - 0x400: Round to nearest even \n   - 0x800: Round toward negative infinity\n   - 0xC00: Round toward positive infinity\n8. Check for inexact result condition (flags & 0x2) with (dwControlMask & 0x10)\n9. If inexact result, extract mantissa using FUN_1001e81e for extended precision\n10. Apply exponent bias adjustment (-1536 decimal, -0x600 hex)\n11. Handle denormalized numbers (exponent < -1074) by setting result to 0.0\n12. For normalized numbers, construct 53-bit mantissa with implicit leading 1\n13. Handle severe underflow (exponent < -1021) with bit-shifting loop\n14. Apply sign correction if original value was negative\n15. Store final result back to *pdValue\n16. Check final exception condition (flags & 0x10) with (dwControlMask & 0x20)\n17. Return true if all exception flags cleared, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\ndwFlags: Floating-point processor status flags with exception indicators\n  Bit 0 (0x01): Overflow flag\n  Bit 1 (0x02): Inexact result flag  \n  Bit 2 (0x04): Underflow flag\n  Bit 3 (0x08): Precision exception flag\n  Bit 4 (0x10): Final exception check flag\npdValue: Pointer to double-precision floating-point value to process\ndwControlMask: Control mask for exception handling\n  Bit 0 (0x01): Enable precision exception handling\n  Bit 2 (0x04): Enable underflow exception handling  \n  Bit 3 (0x08): Enable overflow exception handling\n  Bit 4 (0x10): Enable inexact result handling\n  Bit 5 (0x20): Enable final exception handling\n  Bits 10-11 (0xC00): Rounding mode control\n\nReturns:\ntrue: All exception flags successfully processed and cleared\nfalse: One or more exception flags remain active\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero values at _DAT_10027cf8 bypass precision conversion\n- Denormalized numbers (exponent < -1074) converted to exact 0.0\n- Severe underflow requires iterative bit-shifting with rounding\n- Sign preservation through all precision adjustments\n- Exception handler FUN_1001e91f called for each detected condition\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1F (31): Flag extraction mask for lower 5 bits\n0x600 (1536): IEEE 754 exponent bias adjustment\n0x432 (1074): Minimum normalized exponent threshold  \n0x3FD (1021): Severe underflow threshold requiring bit shifting\n0xC00 (3072): Rounding mode mask (bits 10-11)\n0x10000000000000: Implicit mantissa leading bit (bit 52)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
