      "name": "ClassifyFloatingPointValue",
      "signature": "int ClassifyFloatingPointValue(int nLowBits, uint dwHighBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Classify IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point value by examining bit patterns\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if upper 32-bits equal 0x7FF00000 (positive infinity exponent pattern)\n   If so, check if lower 32-bits are zero for pure positive infinity\n2. Check if upper 32-bits equal 0xFFF00000 (negative infinity exponent pattern)  \n   If so, check if lower 32-bits are zero for pure negative infinity\n3. Extract upper 16-bits from high word and mask with 0x7FF8\n   If result equals 0x7FF8, classify as NaN (quiet bit set in exponent)\n4. Check if masked exponent equals 0x7FF0 (infinity base pattern)\n   If so, verify mantissa bits: test upper word & 0x7FFFF and lower word\n   If mantissa non-zero, classify as subnormal/special infinity case\n5. Return classification value based on detected pattern\n\nParameters:\nnLowBits (int): Lower 32 bits of IEEE 754 double-precision value\ndwHighBits (uint): Upper 32 bits of IEEE 754 double-precision value\n\nReturns:\n0: Normal finite floating-point number\n1: Positive infinity (+\u221e)\n2: Negative infinity (-\u221e)  \n3: NaN (Not a Number) with quiet bit set\n4: Subnormal infinity or special infinity case with non-zero mantissa\n\nSpecial Cases:\nUses IEEE 754 standard bit patterns for classification\nExamines sign bit (bit 63), exponent field (bits 62-52), mantissa (bits 51-0)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7FF00000: Positive infinity exponent pattern (exponent = all 1s, sign = 0)\n0xFFF00000: Negative infinity exponent pattern (exponent = all 1s, sign = 1)\n0x7FF8: NaN pattern with quiet bit (0x7FF0 base + 0x0008 quiet bit)\n0x7FF0: Base infinity exponent pattern (bits 62-52 all 1s)\n0x7FFFF: Mantissa mask for upper word (bits 51-32 of full mantissa)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1cc74c1aae037b1cf063b65efc050353f8bdda371a021018d3ce0ab60357df22",
