      "name": "DispatchFpuCompareHandler",
      "signature": "void DispatchFpuCompareHandler(void * pUnused, void * pDispatchContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Dispatches to FPU comparison handler based on FPU status flags and context type.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Dispatcher - dispatches to function pointer based on FPU comparison\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check dispatch context type byte at offset +0x0E\n2. If type == 0x05, set custom FPU control word with precision bits modified\n3. Otherwise, set default FPU control word 0x133F (double precision, round to nearest)\n4. Store dispatch context pointer at caller's stack frame offset -0x94\n5. Compare input FPU value (ST0) against zero, build status word:\n   - Bit 8: NAN flag\n   - Bit 9: Less than zero flag  \n   - Bit 10: Not equal to zero flag\n   - Bit 14: Equal to zero flag\n6. Extract FPU status index from calculated status (bits 0-2 with sign extension)\n7. Use index to lookup offset from g_abFpuCompareJumpOffsets table\n8. Call handler at pDispatchContext + lookup_offset + 0x10\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (ECX): void* - Unused fastcall parameter\n  pDispatchContext (EDX): void* - Dispatch context structure containing:\n    +0x0E: Type byte (0x05 = special precision mode)\n    +0x10+offset: Function pointer table\n\nReturns: void (dispatches to handler which may return value)\n\nIMPLICIT: in_ST0 (float10) - FPU register containing value to compare\nIMPLICIT: unaff_EBP - Caller's frame pointer for stack variable access\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x05: Special FPU precision type flag\n  0x133F: Default FPU control word (double precision, round to nearest, all exceptions masked)\n  0x3F: FPU control word low byte with default precision\n  0x6f9f0d4c: Jump offset table (g_abFpuCompareJumpOffsets)\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n  Function body shows only 1 instruction in disassembly due to incomplete function \n  bounds - decompiler reads beyond function boundary. The actual code dispatches \n  via indirect jump (FF 23 - JMP [EBX]) which Ghidra cannot fully analyze.",
