      "name": "PerformExtendedPrecisionDivision",
      "signature": "undefined4 PerformExtendedPrecisionDivision(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs extended precision (80-bit) floating-point division using FPU registers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Accept two 80-bit extended precision floating-point values from FPU stack (ST0 and ST1)\n2. Store ST1 (divisor) to stack location [ESP] using FSTP instruction\n3. Store ST0 (dividend) to stack location [ESP + 0xC] using FSTP instruction  \n4. Decompose the 80-bit values into component parts for parameter passing:\n   - Extract low 32-bit mantissa from each operand\n   - Extract high 32-bit mantissa from each operand  \n   - Extract 16-bit exponent and sign from each operand\n5. Call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision with decomposed parameters\n6. Return the result status code from EAX register\n\nParameters:\n\nldDivisor (implicit in ST1): 80-bit extended precision divisor value\nldDividend (implicit in ST0): 80-bit extended precision dividend value  \nIMPLICIT wStackParam: 16-bit parameter passed via stack for extended precision handling\n\nReturns:\n\ndwResult: Status code from division operation\n- Non-zero: Operation completed successfully\n- Zero: Division error or special case detected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nDivision by zero, infinity, NaN, and denormalized number handling is delegated to ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision function.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0xC (12): Stack offset for storing first operand (ST0/dividend)\n0x2C (44): Total stack space allocated for parameter storage and alignment",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
