      "comment": "Processes YUV color space conversion and pixel blitting operations for video rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract format flags from dwFlags to determine color space format (0x70000000 mask)\n2. If YUV420 format detected (0x60000000), halve chroma dimensions and double stride values\n3. Handle pixel alignment for 2-byte and 3-byte formats with boundary adjustments\n4. Calculate source buffer address using dwSrcWidth * nSrcStride + dwSrcX + pixelSize * dwSrcY\n5. Double stride for specific color formats requiring extended alignment (0x20000000, 0x50000000)\n6. Call preprocessing function for format-specific parameter adjustment\n7. Calculate destination buffer addresses for RGB and chroma components\n8. Compute chroma channel offsets based on interlaced vs progressive flag (0x10000)\n9. Process odd-numbered rows first if height is odd and within processing range\n10. Calculate alignment constraints for horizontal pixel processing\n11. Update global processing counter with row count if conditions are met\n12. Process scanlines in pairs using pixel conversion and format handling functions\n13. Handle remaining unaligned pixels with specialized handlers\n14. Call optional post-processing function if enabled and not in test mode\n\nParameters:\ndwSrcX: Source X coordinate in pixels (left edge of source region)\ndwSrcY: Source Y coordinate in pixels (top edge of source region)  \nnSrcStride: Source scanline stride in bytes (row pitch)\ndwSrcWidth: Source width in pixels (horizontal span)\ndwSrcHeight: Source height in pixels (vertical span)\ndwDstX: Destination X coordinate in pixels (left edge of destination)\ndwDstY: Destination Y coordinate in pixels (top edge of destination)\ndwDstWidth: Destination width in pixels (target horizontal span)\ndwDstHeight: Destination height in pixels (target vertical span)\ndwSrcStride2: Secondary source stride for chroma channels\ndwDstStride: Destination scanline stride in bytes (output row pitch)\ndwFlags: Format and control flags (color space, interlacing, test mode)\npPixelFormat: Pointer to pixel format descriptor integer\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value, operates through global buffer pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nYUV420 format (dwFlags & 0x70000000 == 0x60000000): Chroma subsampling applied\n2-byte pixel alignment: X coordinate adjusted to 4-byte boundary for performance\n3-byte pixel alignment: Complex alignment with 3/6/9 pixel offset corrections\nInterlaced processing (dwFlags & 0x10000): Swaps chroma line calculation order\nOdd height processing: Handles extra scanline when height is not even\nTest mode (dwFlags & 0x40000): Disables post-processing for validation\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x70000000 - Color format identification mask for YUV detection\n0x60000000 - YUV420 planar format requiring chroma subsampling\n0x20000000 - Format identifier requiring doubled source stride\n0x50000000 - Alternate format identifier requiring doubled source stride\n0x10000 - Interlaced vs progressive processing control flag\n0x40000 - Test mode flag that disables post-processing operations\n0x80 - Default counter reset value for processing state\n0x2000 - Maximum counter threshold before overflow protection\n\nGlobal Data Access:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent/g_pSrcBufferEnd: Source buffer current and end addresses\ng_pDstBufferCurrent/g_pDstBufferEnd: Destination buffer current and end addresses  \ng_pChromaBufferU/g_pChromaBufferV: Chroma component buffer pointers for U/V channels\ng_pfnScanlineProcessor: Function pointer for scanline processing operations\ng_pdwProcessingCounter: Global processing counter with overflow protection\ng_pfnPixelConverter: Function pointer for pixel format conversion\ng_pfnEvenPixelHandler/g_pfnOddPixelHandler: Specialized pixel alignment handlers\ng_dwAlignmentMask: Bit mask for pixel alignment calculations\ng_dwPostProcessFlag: Enable flag for post-processing operations",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
