      "name": "StandardPixelHandlerSecondary",
      "signature": "undefined StandardPixelHandlerSecondary(undefined4 param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes pixel data in two passes with buffer state preservation and chroma buffer swapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current buffer pointers from globals (src, dst, chroma)\n2. Call pixel processing callback with provided parameter\n3. Advance source buffer pointers by pixel stride\n4. Calculate offset between source buffer positions\n5. Swap chroma U and V buffer pointers (U->dst_end, V->chroma_u)\n6. Call pixel processing callback again for secondary pass\n7. Restore source buffer pointers using calculated offset\n\nParameters:\ndwProcessingParam - Processing parameter passed to the pixel callback function\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies global buffer state as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- unaff_EBX contains preserved destination end pointer from caller\n- unaff_retaddr is reused as second callback parameter (likely optimization artifact)\n- Two-pass design processes pixel pairs for YUV/chroma subsampling\n\nGlobal Variables Modified:\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent (0x100332e0) - Current source buffer position\ng_pSrcBufferEnd (0x100332e4) - Source buffer end position  \ng_pDstBufferCurrent (0x100332e8) - Current destination buffer position\ng_pDstBufferEnd (0x100332ec) - Destination buffer end position\ng_pChromaBufferU (0x100332f0) - Chroma U plane buffer pointer\ng_pChromaBufferV (0x100332f4) - Chroma V plane buffer pointer\ng_pfnPixelProcessCallback (0x10038f74) - Pixel processing callback function pointer\ng_dwPixelStride (0x1003331c) - Bytes to advance per pixel operation",
