      "name": "ExpandIndexedBytesToArgb1555Pixels",
      "signature": "undefined ExpandIndexedBytesToArgb1555Pixels(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Expands 8-bit indexed color bytes to 16-bit ARGB1555 pixels with vertical doubling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pixel count is at least 2 (early exit if less)\n2. Calculate loop iterations as pixelCount / 2 (processes 2 source bytes per iteration)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Read two consecutive source bytes from g_pDstBufferCurrent\n   b. Expand first byte to 32-bit value with pixel duplicated in high/low words + alpha bits\n   c. Expand second byte to 32-bit value with pixel duplicated in high/low words + alpha bits\n   d. Write both expanded values to current scanline (g_pSrcBufferCurrent)\n   e. Write both expanded values to next scanline (g_pSrcBufferCurrent + g_dwPixelStride)\n   f. Advance source pointer by 2 bytes, destination pointer by 8 bytes\n4. Return after processing all pixel pairs\n\nParameters:\npUnused (uint*) - Unused parameter, likely vestigial from function pointer table\ndwPixelCount (uint) - Number of source pixels to process (must be >= 2)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Results written to global buffer pointers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x80008000 - Alpha bits set for both packed ARGB1555 pixels (bit 15 in each 16-bit half)\n0x10 (16) - Shift to duplicate pixel byte into high word position\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\ng_pDstBufferCurrent - Source buffer pointer (8-bit indexed color bytes)\ng_pSrcBufferCurrent - Destination buffer pointer (16-bit ARGB1555 pixels)\ng_dwPixelStride - Scanline stride for vertical pixel doubling",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "NOP",
