      "name": "ProcessYuvColorConversion",
      "signature": "void ProcessYuvColorConversion(uint dwSrcXOffset, uint dwSrcYOffset, int nSrcPitch, uint nSrcWidth, byte * pbMask, int nMaskPitch, uint dwDstOffset, uint dwDstWidth, uint nDstHeight, byte * pbDstBuffer, uint nDstStride, uint dwFormatFlags, int * pnBufferPointers)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes YUV to RGB color conversion with mask-based pixel skipping and format-specific optimizations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract format flags from dwFormatFlags (0x70000000 mask) to determine color format\n2. Adjust parameters for 16-bit modes: halve height, double width and pitch for 0x60000000 format  \n3. Calculate source buffer position using X/Y offsets, pitch, and buffer pointer scaling\n4. Double source width for planar formats (0x20000000, 0x50000000)\n5. Initialize color conversion state for both primary and secondary processing paths\n6. Determine bytes per pixel (1 for simple formats, 2 for complex YUV formats)\n7. Calculate buffer stride increments and chroma channel offsets\n8. Setup destination and chroma buffer pointers based on format flags (0x10000 swaps U/V)\n9. Process main conversion loop for blocks of 16 rows when height > 15\n10. For each row, process 32-pixel blocks when width > 31\n11. Check mask values to determine pixel processing: 0=skip, 1=process Y only, 2=process UV only, 3=process both\n12. Save buffer state, call conversion function, advance pointers, restore state for non-zero mask\n13. Handle remaining pixels in row (1-15 pixels) with single pixel mask check\n14. Advance to next row with calculated row advance offsets\n15. Process remaining partial width (unaligned pixels) if width not aligned to 16\n16. Process remaining partial height (bottom rows) if height not aligned to 16  \n17. Clear MMX state if post-processing enabled and format doesn't suppress clearing\n\nParameters:\ndwSrcXOffset (uint): Source X coordinate offset in pixels\ndwSrcYOffset (uint): Source Y coordinate offset in pixels  \nnSrcPitch (int): Source buffer stride/pitch in bytes\ndwSrcWidth (uint): Source width in pixels to process\npbMask (byte *): Pointer to mask buffer for pixel skipping\nnMaskPitch (int): Mask buffer stride/pitch in bytes\ndwDstOffset (uint): Destination buffer offset in bytes\ndwDstWidth (uint): Destination width in pixels\ndwDstHeight (uint): Destination height in pixels\npbDstBuffer (byte *): Pointer to destination RGB buffer\ndwDstStride (uint): Destination buffer stride in bytes\ndwFormatFlags (uint): Format and processing flags\npnBufferPointers (int *): Array of buffer pointers for conversion state\n\nReturns:\nvoid (performs in-place conversion using global buffer pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Format 0x60000000: 16-bit mode requires parameter doubling/halving\n- Formats 0x20000000/0x50000000: Planar modes need doubled source width  \n- Formats 0x30000000/0x40000000/0x50000000: Complex YUV modes use 2 bytes per pixel\n- Flag 0x10000: Swaps U and V chroma channel buffer order\n- Flag 0x40000: Suppresses MMX state clearing\n- Width/height alignment: Partial blocks handled separately at edges\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x70000000 - Format type mask for extracting color format\n0x60000000 - 16-bit YUV format requiring parameter adjustment\n0x20000000 - Planar format type 1  \n0x50000000 - Planar format type 2\n0x30000000 - Complex YUV format type 1\n0x40000000 - Complex YUV format type 2  \n0x10000 - U/V channel swap flag\n0x40000 - MMX clear suppression flag\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking (assumes valid parameters)\n- Relies on mask buffer to control pixel processing\n- Global buffer pointers must be valid before call\n- MMX state cleared automatically unless suppressed\n\nState Machine:\nState 1: Parameter Setup - Extract format flags and adjust parameters\nState 2: Buffer Calculation - Calculate all buffer pointers and strides  \nState 3: Main Loop - Process 16x32 pixel blocks with mask checking\nState 4: Row Remainder - Handle remaining pixels in each row\nState 5: Height Remainder - Process bottom rows if height not aligned\nState 6: Cleanup - Clear MMX state if required",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
