      "name": "ClearFpuStackAndReturnOne",
      "signature": "float10 ClearFpuStackAndReturnOne(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10",
      "comment": "Clears two entries from the FPU stack and returns the floating-point constant 1.0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pop and discard top FPU stack entry (FSTP ST0)\n2. Pop and discard second FPU stack entry (FSTP ST0)\n3. Load constant 1.0 onto FPU stack (FLD1)\n4. Return with 1.0 in ST0\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  float10 - Always returns 1.0\n\nNotes:\n  This is an FPU cleanup utility that ensures a consistent FPU stack state\n  and returns a default success value (1.0). Used as an error recovery or\n  normalization helper in floating-point computation chains.",
