      "name": "MarkFpuStatusHandled",
      "signature": "void MarkFpuStatusHandled(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Marks FPU special case status as handled without modifying the return value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set status byte at caller's [EBP-0x90] to 1 (mark handled)\n2. Execute OR CL,CL to set processor flags for caller\n3. Return with ST0 unchanged (preserves current FPU value)\n\nParameters:\nNone explicit\nIMPLICIT: EBP from caller's frame (accesses [EBP-0x90] status byte)\nIMPLICIT: CL register (set for flag testing by caller)\nIMPLICIT: ST0 (FPU value passed through unchanged)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Status byte modified, FPU stack unchanged\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called as jump table handler from DispatchFpuCompareHandler\n- Does not pop or modify FPU stack unlike ReturnNegativeInfinityF64\n- Used when FPU comparison result requires no value modification\n\nCallers:\nDispatchFpuCompareHandler - Called via indirect jump table dispatch\n\nClassification: Leaf/internal utility function",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:cf87ce9155410ada78115f0e013bf7b0685d4707d3c3e26731b4b2a32cca4ad5",
