      "name": "MarshalFpuOperandsForDivision",
      "signature": "void MarshalFpuOperandsForDivision(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Marshals FPU stack operands to CPU stack for extended precision division.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Marshals FPU operands to stack for ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 44 bytes (0x2c) on stack for two float10 values plus alignment\n2. Pop ST(0) to Stack[-0x20] as 10-byte extended precision float\n3. Pop ST(1) to Stack[-0x2c] as 10-byte extended precision float  \n4. Call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision with split mantissa/exponent parameters\n5. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ST(0) - First FPU operand (dividend), stored to ldOperandA\n  IMPLICIT ST(1) - Second FPU operand (divisor), stored to ldOperandB\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result returned through FPU stack by callee\n\nAssembly-Only Variables (Phantom):\n  local_2c (Stack[-0x2c]:10) - ldOperandB: Extended precision storage for ST(1)\n  local_20 (Stack[-0x20]:10) - ldOperandA: Extended precision storage for ST(0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2c (44) - Stack allocation: two 10-byte float10 + 12 bytes alignment/padding\n  0x0c (12) - Offset between the two float10 operands on stack\n\nCalled By:\n  ComputeFloatRemainderWithExceptionHandling - For remainder operations with exceptions\n  FUN_10020aec - For single-precision float remainder operations",
