      "name": "PrepareExtendedDivisionOperands",
      "signature": "void PrepareExtendedDivisionOperands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Prepares FPU operands for extended precision division by spilling to stack.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Marshals FPU registers to stack for ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2c (44) bytes of stack space for two float10 operands\n2. Store ST0 (dividend) to stack at [ESP+0x0c] as extended double\n3. Store ST1 (divisor) to stack at [ESP+0x00] as extended double\n4. Call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision with operands on stack\n5. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT ST0 (float10): Dividend value in FPU register\n  IMPLICIT ST1 (float10): Divisor value in FPU register\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result returned via FPU state modification by callee\n\nStack Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field              Description\n  0x00     10     ldDivisor          ST1 spilled to stack (float10)\n  0x0c     10     ldDividend         ST0 spilled to stack (float10)\n  0x16     22     (padding)          Stack alignment\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  local_2c (Stack[-0x2c]:10): Storage for ST1 (divisor) - float10\n  local_20 (Stack[-0x20]:10): Storage for ST0 (dividend) - float10\n\nNote: This is a marshaling thunk that converts FPU register-based operands\nto stack-based parameters expected by ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
