      "name": "BinkDirectSoundHandler",
      "signature": "int BinkDirectSoundHandler(uint * pContext, uint dwSampleRate, uint dwBitsPerSample, uint dwChannelCount, uint dwUnused1, uint dwUnused2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a DirectSound audio handler context for Bink video playback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the context structure (47 DWORDs = 188 bytes) using REP STOSD\n2. Call InitializeDirectSoundInterface to set up the DirectSound system\n3. If initialization fails, return 0 immediately\n4. Calculate audio format parameters (block align, bytes per second)\n5. Set up WAVEFORMAT structure with PCM format tag (0x1)\n6. If DirectSound is already initialized, clean up existing buffer\n7. Calculate buffer duration based on quality setting (100ms or 175ms)\n8. Find optimal buffer multiplier by doubling until >= duration\n9. Create primary DirectSound buffer via IDirectSound::CreateSoundBuffer\n10. Configure audio output with default volume (0x7fff max)\n11. Populate handler vtable with 8 function pointers for playback control\n12. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pContext      - Pointer to 188-byte context structure to initialize\n  dwSampleRate  - Audio sample rate in Hz (e.g., 44100, 22050)\n  dwBitsPerSample - Bits per audio sample (8 or 16)\n  dwChannelCount  - Number of audio channels (1=mono, 2=stereo)\n  dwUnused1     - Reserved parameter (not used)\n  dwUnused2     - Reserved parameter (not used)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE)  - Context successfully initialized with DirectSound buffer\n  0 (FALSE) - Initialization failed (DirectSound unavailable or buffer creation failed)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2f (47)     - DWORD count for context structure (47 * 4 = 188 bytes)\n  0x14 (20)     - DirectSound buffer description size\n  0x1           - WAVE_FORMAT_PCM format tag\n  0x4b (75)     - Additional buffer duration for high quality (75ms)\n  0x64 (100)    - Base buffer duration (100ms)\n  0x10624dd3    - Magic multiplier for division by 1000\n  0x7fff        - Maximum volume level (32767)\n  0x180e0       - Buffer flags (DSBCAPS_PRIMARYBUFFER | DSBCAPS_CTRLVOLUME | etc)\n\nHandler Vtable (offsets 0x00-0x1c):\n  +0x00: 0x1001c440 - Audio data copy handler\n  +0x04: 0x1001c700 - Buffer lock handler\n  +0x08: 0x1001c750 - Buffer unlock handler\n  +0x0c: 0x1001c7d0 - Volume control handler\n  +0x10: 0x1001c800 - Pan control handler\n  +0x14: 0x1001c8c0 - Status query handler\n  +0x18: 0x1001c830 - Play/stop control handler\n  +0x1c: 0x1001c930 - Cleanup handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:607c5f168bd9d39a3687a53afff9e59ea8c41590aae60b4bc96c6c5706351779",
